COLLDATA("qencen","en",[[322,"§Ta-Seen\nSee: Alif-Laam-Meem."],[323,"§Ta-Seen-Meem\nSee: Alif-Laam-Meem."],[324,"§Taurah\n‘Taurah’ means the following five books of the Bible mentioned in the Jewish and Christian history:\n1. Genesis.\n2. Exodus.\n3. Leviticus.\n4. Numbers.\n5. Deuteronomy.\nSome scholars are of the opinion that these five books of the Old Testament were revealed to Musa(as) by Allah(swt). But when we study these books it becomes clear that this cannot be true because they have descriptions of some historical events which happened after the death of Musa(as). For example at the end of the book of Deuteronomy, the death of Musa(as) is described which proves that this part was not revealed to Musa(as) but was written by someone else and added later on.\nThat is why some of the scholars have started saying that Taurah means the ten commandments which were given to Musa(as) on stone tablets and the instructions given to him over the next forty years which are scattered in the Old Testament. This is the reason why the Holy Quran has nowhere confirmed these five books. It only says that Allah(swt) had given the book to Musa(as) and Haroon(as):\n﴿وَآتَيْنَاهُمَا الْكِتَابَ الْمُسْتَبِينَ ١١٧﴾\nAnd We gave them the explicit Scripture.\n[As-Saffat: 117]\nقُلْ مَنْ أَنزَلَ الْكِتَابَ الَّذِي جَاءَ بِهِ مُوسَىٰ نُورًا وَهُدًى لِّلنَّاسِ ۖ تَجْعَلُونَهُ قَرَاطِيسَ تُبْدُونَهَا وَتُخْفُونَ كَثِيرًا ۖ\nSay, \"Who revealed the Scripture that Moses brought as light and guidance to the people? You [Jews] make it into pages, disclosing [some of] it and concealing much.”\n[Al-An’am: 91]\n‘Taurah’ is the name of the book which is mentioned again and again in the Holy Quran and it has also been indicated in many places that the Jewish scholars have distorted it. But there are still a few parts of the divine revelations in it and these are the ‘light’ and ‘guidance’ described in the above verse of the Holy Quran. These are the only parts which are confirmed by the Holy Quran and not the five books which the Jews and Christians attribute to Musa(as). Because the Holy Quran is the Last Book of Revelation of Allah(swt), anything which goes against it stands annulled.\nAs for the remaining 34 books which are part of the Old Testament, the Jewish and Christian scholars themselves agree that they were written during various periods and ’Azra Kahin’ collected them in one place. The 34 books are:\n6. Joshua, 7. Judges, 8. Ruth, 9. 1 Samuel, 10. 2 Samuel, 11. 1 Kings, 12. 2 Kings, 13. 1 Chronicles, 14. 2 Chronicles, 15. Ezra, 16. Nehemiah, 17. Esther, 18. Job, 19. Psalm, 20. Proverbs, 21. Ecclesiastes, 22. Song of Songs, 23. Isaiah, 24. Jeremiah, 25. Lamentations, 26. Ezekiel, 27. Daniel, 28. Hosea, 29. Joel, 30. Amos, 31. Obadiah, 32. Jonah, 33. Micah, 34. Nahum, 35. Habakkuk, 36. Zephaniah, 37. Haggai, 38. Zechariah and 39. Malachi.\nIn this way along with the first five books, the total number of books in the Old Testament becomes 39."],[325,"§Tawba\n‘Tawba’ means ‘repentance’ or ‘turn back’ or ‘Ruzu’. It is a very important part of Islamic teachings because though man is born honest by nature, he is disobedient, arrogant and despotic in his actions. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَآتَاكُم مِّن كُلِّ مَا سَأَلْتُمُوهُ ۚ وَإِن تَعُدُّوا نِعْمَتَ اللَّـهِ لَا تُحْصُوهَا ۗ إِنَّ الْإِنسَانَ لَظَلُومٌ كَفَّارٌ ٣٤﴾\nAnd He gave you from all you asked of Him. And if you should count the favor of Allah, you could not enumerate them. Indeed, mankind is [generally] most unjust and ungrateful.\n[Ibraheem: 34]\n﴿إِنَّا عَرَضْنَا الْأَمَانَةَ عَلَى السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَالْجِبَالِ فَأَبَيْنَ أَن يَحْمِلْنَهَا وَأَشْفَقْنَ مِنْهَا وَحَمَلَهَا الْإِنسَانُ ۖ إِنَّهُ كَانَ ظَلُومًا جَهُولًا ٧٢﴾\nIndeed, we offered the Trust to the heavens and the earth and the mountains, and they declined to bear it and feared it; but man [undertook to] bear it. Indeed, he was unjust and ignorant.\n[Al-Ahzab: 72]\nOne reason for man being unjust is the satan:\nإِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ لِلْإِنسَانِ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِينٌ\nIndeed Satan, to man, is a manifest enemy.\n[Yusuf: 5]\nOn one hand, man is ignorant and unjust because he undertook to bear the trust which was declined by the earth, sky and the mountains. On the other hand the satan is forever after him trying to mislead him. Under these conditions it is not surprising that man is continuously sinning because the satan is trying to make him disobey Allah(swt) at each and every step and before this he had succeeded in making even Adam(as) disobey Allah(swt):\n﴿فَوَسْوَسَ إِلَيْهِ الشَّيْطَانُ قَالَ يَا آدَمُ هَلْ أَدُلُّكَ عَلَىٰ شَجَرَةِ الْخُلْدِ وَمُلْكٍ لَّا يَبْلَىٰ ١٢٠ فَأَكَلَا مِنْهَا فَبَدَتْ لَهُمَا سَوْآتُهُمَا وَطَفِقَا يَخْصِفَانِ عَلَيْهِمَا مِن وَرَقِ الْجَنَّةِ ۚ وَعَصَىٰ آدَمُ رَبَّهُ فَغَوَىٰ ١٢١﴾\nThen Satan whispered to him; he said, \"O Adam, shall I direct you to the tree of eternity and possession that will not deteriorate?\" And Adam and his wife ate of it, and their private parts became apparent to them, and they began to fasten over themselves from the leaves of Paradise. And Adam disobeyed his Lord and erred.\n[Ta-Ha: 120, 121]\nWhen men started going astray, Allah(swt) opened the doors of His mercy with the help of ‘Tawba’ and said to his slaves:\n﴿قُلْ يَا عِبَادِيَ الَّذِينَ أَسْرَفُوا عَلَىٰ أَنفُسِهِمْ لَا تَقْنَطُوا مِن رَّحْمَةِ اللَّـهِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًا ۚ إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْغَفُورُ الرَّحِيمُ ٥٣﴾\nSay, \"O My servants who have transgressed against themselves [by sinning], do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\"\n[Az-Zumar: 53]\nAt one place Allah(swt) commands men to repent:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا تُوبُوا إِلَى اللَّهِ تَوْبَةً نَّصُوحًا عَسَىٰ رَبُّكُمْ أَن يُكَفِّرَ عَنكُمْ سَيِّئَاتِكُمْ وَيُدْخِلَكُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِن تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ يَوْمَ لَا يُخْزِي اللَّهُ النَّبِيَّ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَهُ ۖ\nO you who have believed, repent to Allah with sincere repentance. Perhaps your Lord will remove from you your misdeeds and admit you into gardens beneath which rivers flow [on] the Day when Allah will not disgrace the Prophet and those who believed with him.\n[At-Tahrim: 8]\nIn the above verse, the Arabic word ‘taubatan Nasooha’ has been used which means tauba or repentance done with a sincere heart. The following are the conditions for such repentance:\n1. The person repenting for a sin should forever give up that sin and determine and strive not to go near that sin ever again.\n2. He should be ashamed before Allah(swt) for the sin which he has committed.\n3. If the sin is against other people, then he should ask their forgiveness and if he has taken somebody’s wealth, he should return it.\nThis sort of repentance is called ‘taubatun Nasooha’ and surely one who has repented truly and sincerely can never do that sin again and if he does it by mistake, he will do ‘tawba’(repent) immediately. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَإِذَا جَاءَكَ الَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِآيَاتِنَا فَقُلْ سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكُمْ ۖ كَتَبَ رَبُّكُمْ عَلَىٰ نَفْسِهِ الرَّحْمَةَ ۖ أَنَّهُ مَنْ عَمِلَ مِنكُمْ سُوءًا بِجَهَالَةٍ ثُمَّ تَابَ مِن بَعْدِهِ وَأَصْلَحَ فَأَنَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ٥٤﴾\nAnd when those come to you who believe in Our verses, say, \"Peace be upon you. Your Lord has decreed upon Himself mercy: that any of you who does wrong out of ignorance and then repents after that and corrects himself - indeed, He is Forgiving and Merciful.\"\n[Al-An’am: 54]\nDoing ‘tawba’ is the way of the prophets. For example Adam(as) repented:\n﴿فَتَلَقَّىٰ آدَمُ مِن رَّبِّهِ كَلِمَاتٍ فَتَابَ عَلَيْهِ ۚ إِنَّهُ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ ٣٧﴾\nThen Adam received from his Lord [some] words, and He accepted his repentance. Indeed, it is He who is the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.\n[Al-Baqara: 37]\nIbraheem(as) was also among the ones who repented. Ibraheem(as) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿رَبَّنَا تَقَبَّلْ مِنَّا ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ ١٢٧ رَبَّنَا وَاجْعَلْنَا مُسْلِمَيْنِ لَكَ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِنَا أُمَّةً مُّسْلِمَةً لَّكَ وَأَرِنَا مَنَاسِكَنَا وَتُبْ عَلَيْنَا ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ ١٢٨﴾\n\"Our Lord, accept [this] from us. Indeed You are the Hearing, the Knowing. Our Lord, and make us Muslims [in submission] to You and from our descendants a Muslim nation [in submission] to You. And show us our rites and accept our repentance. Indeed, You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.”\n[Al-Baqara: 127, 128]\nMusa(as) had also repented:\nفَلَمَّا تَجَلَّىٰ رَبُّهُ لِلْجَبَلِ جَعَلَهُ دَكًّا وَخَرَّ مُوسَىٰ صَعِقًا ۚ فَلَمَّا أَفَاقَ قَالَ سُبْحَانَكَ تُبْتُ إِلَيْكَ وَأَنَا أَوَّلُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ\nBut when his Lord appeared to the mountain, He rendered it level, and Moses fell unconscious. And when he awoke, he said, \"Exalted are You! I have repented to You, and I am the first of the believers.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 143]\nAnd then Allah(swt) commands all the believers to repent:\nوَتُوبُوا إِلَى اللَّهِ جَمِيعًا أَيُّهَ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ\nAnd turn to Allah in repentance, all of you, O believers, that you might succeed.\n[An-Nur: 31]\nDoing ‘tawba’ is also a form of worship. Therefore it is for Allah(swt) alone. Doing ‘tawba’ before someone else is equivalent to ascribing partners to Him. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿أَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّـهَ هُوَ يَقْبَلُ التَّوْبَةَ عَنْ عِبَادِهِ وَيَأْخُذُ الصَّدَقَاتِ وَأَنَّ اللَّـهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ ١٠٤﴾\nDo they not know that it is Allah who accepts repentance from His servants and receives charities and that it is Allah who is the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful?\n[At-Tawba: 104]\n﴿وَهُوَ الَّذِي يَقْبَلُ التَّوْبَةَ عَنْ عِبَادِهِ وَيَعْفُو عَنِ السَّيِّئَاتِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تَفْعَلُونَ ٢٥﴾\nAnd it is He who accepts repentance from his servants and pardons misdeeds, and He knows what you do.\n[Ash-Shura: 25]\nIt is clear from the above verses that just as all forms of worship are for Allah(swt) alone, even ‘tawba’ should be done only before Allah(swt). He(swt) is the One who accepts repentance and forgives the sins of His slaves. He(swt) has no partners. So, if anyone does ‘tawba’ before anyone other than Allah(swt) then he has done shirk and shirk is the greatest of all sins which Allah(swt) shall never forgive."],[326,"§Tawheed\n‘Tawheed’ means belief in the Oneness of Allah(swt). It is the basic and special teaching of Islam. All the prophets have preached ‘tawheed’. But the tribes of those prophets either forgot the instruction of monotheism, or distorted it and as a result went astray. Therefore, Islam has been sent as the last, pure, comprehensive, refined and complete religion for the entire mankind till Doomsday. The Holy Quran and the sahih hadith have all the detailed explanations to prevent mankind from straying once again.\nHere we give a detailed description of the different aspects of ‘Tawheed’ in the light of the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith:\n‘Tawheed’ has three essential elements:\nFirst element: ‘Tawheed’ which means the belief that this world has been created by One Allah(swt). He(swt) has no partners in it, He(swt) alone is governing it, He(swt) is the Sustainer of all the creatures and He(swt) alone will destroy it one day. That is, whatever is happening in this world is as per the orders of Allah(swt). The Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ اللَّـهُ الَّذِي خَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ فِي سِتَّةِ أَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوَىٰ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ يُغْشِي اللَّيْلَ النَّهَارَ يَطْلُبُهُ حَثِيثًا وَالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ وَالنُّجُومَ مُسَخَّرَاتٍ بِأَمْرِهِ ۗ أَلَا لَهُ الْخَلْقُ وَالْأَمْرُ ۗ تَبَارَكَ اللَّـهُ رَبُّ الْعَالَمِينَ ٥٤﴾\nIndeed, your Lord is Allah, who created the heavens and earth in six days and then established Himself above the Throne. He covers the night with the day, [another night] chasing it rapidly; and [He created] the sun, the moon, and the stars, subjected by His command. Unquestionably, His is the creation and the command; blessed is Allah, Lord of the worlds.\n[Al-A’raf: 54]\n﴿قُلِ اللَّـهُمَّ مَالِكَ الْمُلْكِ تُؤْتِي الْمُلْكَ مَن تَشَاءُ وَتَنزِعُ الْمُلْكَ مِمَّن تَشَاءُ وَتُعِزُّ مَن تَشَاءُ وَتُذِلُّ مَن تَشَاءُ ۖ بِيَدِكَ الْخَيْرُ ۖ إِنَّكَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ ٢٦﴾\nSay, \"O Allah, Owner of Sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You will and You take sovereignty away from whom You will. You honor whom You will and You humble whom You will. In Your hand is [all] good. Indeed, You are over all things competent.\n[Al-i-Imran: 26]\nAllah(swt) says in the Holy Quran that He(swt) alone is the Creator of this entire Creation and He(swt) has no partners in it. What have the others created?\n﴿هَـٰذَا خَلْقُ اللَّـهِ فَأَرُونِي مَاذَا خَلَقَ الَّذِينَ مِن دُونِهِ ۚ بَلِ الظَّالِمُونَ فِي ضَلَالٍ مُّبِينٍ ١١﴾\nThis is the creation of Allah. So show Me what those other than Him have created. Rather, the wrongdoers are in clear error.\n[Luqman: 11]\n‘Tawheed’ or ‘monotheism’ is inherent in human nature because when Allah(swt) had created Adam(as), He(swt) took a promise from our souls that He(swt) is our Lord. And Allah(swt) has made countless signs in His Creation which clearly prove that He(swt) alone is the Creator. That is why if it was asked of the disbelievers of Makkah as to who created the earth and the skies, they would reply:\n﴿وَلَئِن سَأَلْتَهُم مَّنْ خَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ لَيَقُولُنَّ اللَّـهُ ۚ قُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلَّـهِ ۚ بَلْ أَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ٢٥﴾\nAnd if you asked them, \"Who created the heavens and earth?\" they would surely say, \"Allah.\" Say, \"[All] praise is [due] to Allah \"; but most of them do not know.\n[Luqman: 25]\nAnd even if someone denies that Allah(swt) is the Lord, it is only a delusion. Everyone knows in his heart of hearts that Allah(swt) is the One God and Lord of the entire Creation. In case of these deluded people the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَجَحَدُوا بِهَا وَاسْتَيْقَنَتْهَا أَنفُسُهُمْ ظُلْمًا وَعُلُوًّا ۚ فَانظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُفْسِدِينَ ١٤﴾\nAnd they rejected them, while their [inner] selves were convinced thereof, out of injustice and haughtiness. So see how was the end of the corrupters.\n[An-Naml: 14]\nThen, the Holy Quran questions such people:\n﴿أَمْ خُلِقُوا مِنْ غَيْرِ شَيْءٍ أَمْ هُمُ الْخَالِقُونَ ٣٥ أَمْ خَلَقُوا السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ ۚ بَل لَّا يُوقِنُونَ ٣٦﴾\nOr were they created by nothing, or were they the creators [of themselves]? Or did they create the heavens and the earth? Rather, they are not certain.\n[At-Tur: 35, 36]\nAn Arabic saying is very popular that the dung of a camel is proof of a camel and its footprints show the direction it has taken. So, aren’t these star-studded sky and vast earth proof of the existence of Allah(swt)?\nSecond element: This is ‘Tawheed-e-Uluhiya’ which means only Allah(swt) is worthy of worship. Worshipping someone other than Allah(swt) is the greatest sin called shirk which Allah(swt) will never forgive. The focal point of the preachings of all the prophets was ‘tawheed’ or ‘monotheism’. The Holy Quran says:\nوَلَقَدْ بَعَثْنَا فِي كُلِّ أُمَّةٍ رَّسُولًا أَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ وَاجْتَنِبُوا الطَّاغُوتَ\nAnd We certainly sent into every nation a messenger, [saying], \"Worship Allah and avoid Taghut.\"\n[An-Nahl: 36]\n﴿وَمَا أَرْسَلْنَا مِن قَبْلِكَ مِن رَّسُولٍ إِلَّا نُوحِي إِلَيْهِ أَنَّهُ لَا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا أَنَا فَاعْبُدُونِ ٢٥﴾\nAnd We sent not before you any messenger except that We revealed to him that, \"There is no deity except Me, so worship Me.\"\n[Al-Anbiya: 25]\nNuh, Hud, Saleh, Shuaib, Musa, Isa(as) and Muhammad(saws), all preached the essential message of ‘Tawheed’. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿لَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ فَقَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّـهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَـٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ إِنِّي أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ٥٩﴾\nWe had certainly sent Noah to his people, and he said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him. Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a tremendous Day.\n[Al-A’raf: 59]\n﴿وَإِلَىٰ عَادٍ أَخَاهُمْ هُودًا ۗ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّـهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَـٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ ۚ أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ٦٥﴾\nAnd to the 'Aad [We sent] their brother Hud. He said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him. Then will you not fear Him?\"\n[Al-A’raf: 65]\nوَإِلَىٰ ثَمُودَ أَخَاهُمْ صَالِحًا ۗ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ\nAnd to the Thamud [We sent] their brother Salih. He said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him.\n[Al-A’raf: 73]\n‘Tawheed’ is the most essential and basic instruction of Islam and the result of all our actions is dependent on it. If we let go of ‘Tawheed’ we stray towards shirk which nullifies all our good deeds.\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ أُوحِيَ إِلَيْكَ وَإِلَى الَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِكَ لَئِنْ أَشْرَكْتَ لَيَحْبَطَنَّ عَمَلُكَ وَلَتَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْخَاسِرِينَ ٦٥﴾\nAnd it was already revealed to you and to those before you that if you should associate [anything] with Allah, your work would surely become worthless, and you would surely be among the losers.\"\n[Az-Zumar: 65]\nThird element: ‘Asma wa Sifat’; that is, realizing that Allah(swt) is unique in his attributes and excellent qualities and not attribute partners to Him in any of His attributes or compare anyone to Allah(swt). Accept the names used by Allah(swt) for Himself and the names used by the prophets as they are. In the same way we should accept the qualities of Allah(swt) which He(swt) has described and have been described by the prophets without any distortions. That is ‘tawheed’. Allah(swt) says about Himself in the Holy Quran:\n﴿فَاطِرُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۚ جَعَلَ لَكُم مِّنْ أَنفُسِكُمْ أَزْوَاجًا وَمِنَ الْأَنْعَامِ أَزْوَاجًا ۖ يَذْرَؤُكُمْ فِيهِ ۚ لَيْسَ كَمِثْلِهِ شَيْءٌ ۖ وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْبَصِيرُ ١١﴾\n[He is] Creator of the heavens and the earth. He has made for you from yourselves, mates, and among the cattle, mates; He multiplies you thereby. There is nothing like unto Him, and He is the Hearing, the Seeing.\n[Ash-Shura: 11]\nThat is, none can be compared with Him in His special qualities and attributes. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَلِلَّـهِ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَىٰ فَادْعُوهُ بِهَا ۖ وَذَرُوا الَّذِينَ يُلْحِدُونَ فِي أَسْمَائِهِ ۚ سَيُجْزَوْنَ مَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ ١٨٠﴾\nAnd to Allah belong the best names, so invoke Him by them. And leave [the company of] those who practice deviation concerning His names. They will be recompensed for what they have been doing.\n[Al-A’raf: 180]\nAllah(swt) has countless names. Ninety-nine names have been mentioned in the sahih hadith. (Sahih Bukhari, 2736 and Sahih Muslim, 2677)\nIn some books the descriptions of these names also have been given but some scholars feel that this is not correct but that some commentators have added their own versions. (See: Tirmizi, 3574; Ibn-Majah, 3861)\nMost of the scholars are of the opinion that the knowledge of the actual number of names of Allah(swt) is with Him alone. He(swt) has given us a part of this knowledge. The ancient tribes have committed shirk in the matter of this ‘tawheed’ namely ‘Asma wa Sifat’. For example, the idolators made the idol Uzza after the name ‘Aziz’ of Allah(swt) and started worshipping it. In the same way they made the idol ‘Manat’ after the name ‘Mannan’ of Allah(swt) and started worshipping it. Among the attributes of Allah(swt), one is that He(swt) creates us, gives us our livelihood and other things and gives us life and death. Now, if we attribute any of these things to someone other than Allah(swt), it will be ‘shirk’.\nEven in the Indian ideology, one God has many forms. But the ignorant have depicted the various forms as various gods and started worshipping them. In this way, polytheism crept into the Indian culture and Indra, Varun, Vishnu, Prajapati became gods and started being worshipped. Right from Rigved to Upanishad and Mahabharat Brahma who had many attributes became the symbol of Advaitavad. The Holy Quran is the only book which clearly and unambiguously explains the concept of ‘Tawheed’ and wherever there is a chance of ‘shirk’, it warns us immediately so that only Allah(swt) is worshipped on this earth and the concept of ‘Tawheed’ never dies down. This concept is explained in various places but we have presented here the three elements of ‘Tawheed’."],[327,"§Tayammam\n‘Tayammam’ is the alternative for ablution or ‘wudu’. That is, if water is not available or cannot be used for some reason, then one can perform ‘tayammam’ and offer salah. As the Holy Quran says at one place:\nوَإِن كُنتُم مَّرْضَىٰ أَوْ عَلَىٰ سَفَرٍ أَوْ جَاءَ أَحَدٌ مِّنكُم مِّنَ الْغَائِطِ أَوْ لَامَسْتُمُ النِّسَاءَ فَلَمْ تَجِدُوا مَاءً فَتَيَمَّمُوا صَعِيدًا طَيِّبًا فَامْسَحُوا بِوُجُوهِكُمْ وَأَيْدِيكُم مِّنْهُ ۚ مَا يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ لِيَجْعَلَ عَلَيْكُم مِّنْ حَرَجٍ وَلَٰكِن يُرِيدُ لِيُطَهِّرَكُمْ وَلِيُتِمَّ نِعْمَتَهُ عَلَيْكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ\nBut if you are ill or on a journey or one of you comes from the place of relieving himself or you have contacted women and do not find water, then seek clean earth and wipe over your faces and hands with it. Allah does not intend to make difficulty for you, but He intends to purify you and complete His favor upon you that you may be grateful.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 6]\nThe description of ‘tayammam’ in the sahih hadith is that you touch the stone or sand or mud or earth with both the hands and then wipe the hands over the arms and face.\nAs explained in the above verse, after doing ‘tayammam’ namaz can be offered just as it can be offered after doing ‘wudu’ even if the person is in a state of ritual impurity, if the person is sick (and the sickness may be aggravated on using water) or water is not available. But when water becomes available, then the tayammam is no longer valid and it becomes compulsory to perform the ‘wudu’ or ablution."],[328,"§Tazeer\n‘Tazeer’ is to stop or forbid doing something. What is meant by ‘Tazeer’ here is to stop people from committing a crime for which no punishment has been designated under the Islamic law. The punishment given by the court in case of such a crime is called ‘Tazeer’. The court decides the punishment in this case. From this we understand the comprehensiveness of Islamic law. But it is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“No one should be given more than ten lashes except in the case of the ‘had’ punishments of Allah(swt).”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 6848 and Sahih Muslim, 1708)\nWe can only say about this that it was in connection with some special case because through ‘Tazeer’ someone can even be hanged. For example, spies who pose a danger to the country, or drug-dealers who are a danger to the society etc. We have some examples from the lives of the companions of the Holy Prophet(saws) in which the punishment was more than ten whip-lashes."],[329,"§Teachings for good behavior\nSee “Quranic teachings about good behavior.”"],[330,"§Three people who were left behind\nIn the Holy Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-118, three persons have been mentioned whose repentance was accepted by Allah(swt). They were: Mararah bin Ar-Rabi`a, Ka`b bin Malik and Hilal bin Umayyah. The detailed description is given in Sahih Muslim as follows:\nIt is narrated by Ka`b bin Malik that he stayed back during the battle of Tabuk which he had never done in other battles even though he was hale and hearty. He had no problem but stayed back only due to laziness. More than eighty people had stayed back. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came back from the expedition of Tabuk, all those people came forward with various excuses. The Holy Quran says about this:\n﴿يَحْلِفُونَ لَكُمْ لِتَرْضَوْا عَنْهُمْ ۖ فَإِن تَرْضَوْا عَنْهُمْ فَإِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَا يَرْضَىٰ عَنِ الْقَوْمِ الْفَاسِقِينَ ٩٦﴾\nThey swear to you so that you might be satisfied with them. But if you should be satisfied with them - indeed, Allah is not satisfied with a defiantly disobedient people.\n[At-Tawba: 96]\nKa`b bin Malik truthfully told the Holy Prophet(saws) that he had no excuse for not accompanying the Holy Prophet(saws) on the expedition of Tabuk. The Holy Prophet(saws) said that he has said the truth and Allah(swt) will decide the matter. The other Muslims were instructed not to talk or do salam to these three people and not even to reply to their salam. Hilal bin Umayyah and Mararah bin Ar-Rabi`a shut themselves up in their homes and wept continuously while Ka`b bin Malik roamed the streets of Madina. Forty days passed this way and their wives were also asked to leave them and life became very lonely and unbearable as the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَعَلَى الثَّلَاثَةِ الَّذِينَ خُلِّفُوا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا ضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْأَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ أَنفُسُهُمْ وَظَنُّوا أَن لَّا مَلْجَأَ مِنَ اللَّـهِ إِلَّا إِلَيْهِ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ لِيَتُوبُوا ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ ١١٨﴾\n(He turned in mercy also) to the three who were left behind; (they felt guilty) to such a degree that the earth seemed constrained to them, for all its spaciousness, and their (very) souls seemed straitened to them,- and they perceived that there is no fleeing from Allah (and no refuge) but to Himself. Then He turned to them, that they might repent: for Allah is Oft-Returning, Most Merciful.\n[At-Tawba: 118]\nWhen Ka`b bin Malik was in this state he got a letter from the king of Ghassan who was a Christian. The king asked Ka`b bin Malik to come to him as the Holy Prophet(saws) had treated him very badly and that the king would give him all sorts of comforts. Ka`b bin Malik threw the letter into the fire saying that this was the second test.\nFinally after fifty days the following verse was revealed in which Allah(swt) commanded the Holy Prophet(saws) to accept the repentance of these three people:\n﴿لَّقَد تَّابَ اللَّـهُ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ وَالْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالْأَنصَارِ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ مِن بَعْدِ مَا كَادَ يَزِيغُ قُلُوبُ فَرِيقٍ مِّنْهُمْ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ إِنَّهُ بِهِمْ رَءُوفٌ رَّحِيمٌ ١١٧ وَعَلَى الثَّلَاثَةِ الَّذِينَ خُلِّفُوا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا ضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْأَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ أَنفُسُهُمْ وَظَنُّوا أَن لَّا مَلْجَأَ مِنَ اللَّـهِ إِلَّا إِلَيْهِ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ لِيَتُوبُوا ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ ١١٨﴾\nAllah has already forgiven the Prophet and the Muhajireen and the Ansar who followed him in the hour of difficulty after the hearts of a party of them had almost inclined [to doubt], and then He forgave them. Indeed, He was to them Kind and Merciful. And [He also forgave] the three who were left behind [and regretted their error] to the point that the earth closed in on them in spite of its vastness and their souls confined them and they were certain that there is no refuge from Allah except in Him. Then He turned to them so they could repent. Indeed, Allah is the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.\n[At-Tawba: 117, 118]\nKa`b bin Malik says that it was the biggest favour of Allah(swt) upon him after Islam, that he had spoken the truth in front of the Holy Prophet(saws). If he had spoken a lie or given a false excuse, then he also would have been destroyed like the others who had lied and been destroyed and had been called evil by Allah(swt). (See: Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-95; Sahih Bukhari, 4418 and Sahih Muslim, 2769)\n(For more information see ‘Tabook’)"],[331,"§Toor\n‘Toor’ is the name of a mountain which is in the southern region of the desert of Sinai. The Bay of Aqba is to the east and the Bay of Suwais is to the west. It is now called the Musa mountain. The ground of ‘Tuwa’ where Allah(swt) gave Musa(as) the Taurah is in the valley of ‘Toor’. Holding this mountain over their hands, a promise was taken from the Bani-Israel that they would hold firmly to the teachings of the Taurah and not let go of them. But due to their distorted nature, they neglected the teachings of the Taurah and instead of the worship of the One True Lord Allah(swt), started worshipping countless gods and goddesses. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَإِذْ أَخَذْنَا مِيثَاقَكُمْ وَرَفَعْنَا فَوْقَكُمُ الطُّورَ خُذُوا مَا آتَيْنَاكُم بِقُوَّةٍ وَاذْكُرُوا مَا فِيهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ ٦٣﴾\nAnd [recall] when We took your covenant, [O Children of Israel, to abide by the Torah] and We raised over you the mount, [saying], \"Take what We have given you with determination and remember what is in it that perhaps you may become righteous.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 63]\n﴿وَنَادَيْنَاهُ مِن جَانِبِ الطُّورِ الْأَيْمَنِ وَقَرَّبْنَاهُ نَجِيًّا ٥٢﴾\nAnd We called him from the side of the mount at [his] right and brought him near, confiding [to him].\n[Maryam: 52]"],[332,"§Trade\nTrade has been given a very important place in the Islamic social order because it is the back-bone of the economy. In the Islamic teachings, trade has been encouraged and its importance can be gauged from the fact that it has been regarded as equivalent to jihad:\nعَلِمَ أَن سَيَكُونُ مِنكُم مَّرْضَىٰ ۙ وَآخَرُونَ يَضْرِبُونَ فِي الْأَرْضِ يَبْتَغُونَ مِن فَضْلِ اللَّهِ ۙ وَآخَرُونَ يُقَاتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ۖ فَاقْرَءُوا مَا تَيَسَّرَ مِنْهُ\nHe has known that there will be among you those who are ill and others traveling throughout the land seeking [something] of the bounty of Allah and others fighting for the cause of Allah.\n[Al-Muzzammil: 20]\n“Sayyidina Raafi' ibn Khadeej (ra) narrates that a person (once) enquired from the Prophet(saws) as to which income was better and more clean. (What was a better way of earning one's livelihood)? \"The one who works with his hands, and every trade that was (done) with honesty,\" replied the Messenger of Allah (saws).” (Musnad Ahmad)\nOn the other hand those people have been severely condemned who take up begging as a means of livelihood be it on streets or as attendants of the graves and delude themselves by saying that they have full faith and trust in Allah(swt). These people will scratch their faces on the Day of Resurrection such that the flesh comes off.\nIslam preaches that we should earn money through honest means and keep away from dishonest and wrong ways and have faith that we shall get whatever we are destined to get. (See: Ibn-Majah: 2142 and Haakim,2:3)\nAmong the basic teachings related to trade in Islam, one is to make sure that the money earned is through lawful means and then extreme care should be taken to see that the money earned is spent in the right way. If money is earned through wrong means, it becomes ‘haram’ and if not spent according to the rules of Islam, its account has to be given on the Day of Judgement.\nWhile most of the forms of trade are lawful in Islam, some which pose a danger to the society are forbidden or haram. A trade in which the rich become richer but the poor become poorer is haram in Islam. These harmful trades have been divided into two:\n1. One is trade based on interest. This is unlawful in Islam in all forms. That is why the disbelievers of Islam had said:\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قَالُوا إِنَّمَا الْبَيْعُ مِثْلُ الرِّبَا ۗ وَأَحَلَّ اللَّهُ الْبَيْعَ وَحَرَّمَ الرِّبَا ۚ\nThat is because they say, \"Trade is [just] like interest.\" But Allah has permitted trade and has forbidden interest.\n[Al-Baqara: 275]\n2. In the second category come the trades which are harmful to the society. These are totally haram in Islam.\nIn fact, the disbelievers of Arabia considered all forms of trade to be lawful even if it was harmful to the society. They were only concerned about their well-being and were least bothered about others. In the matter of trade, Islamic scholars are of the opinion that economy decides the prosperity of a state. That is why the trades which are harmful to the society are unlawful. For example: Interest, which has been described under ‘Interest’.\nTrade which is forbidden in Islam is described briefly here:\ni.) Cheating in the matter of measurements: Since ancient times people have cheated in the matter of measuring out various things. Even the Arabs indulged in this. The Holy Quran condemns and warns such people of a day when Allah(swt) shall take account of their deeds. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَيْلٌ لِّلْمُطَفِّفِينَ ١ الَّذِينَ إِذَا اكْتَالُوا عَلَى النَّاسِ يَسْتَوْفُونَ ٢ وَإِذَا كَالُوهُمْ أَو وَّزَنُوهُمْ يُخْسِرُونَ ٣ أَلَا يَظُنُّ أُولَـٰئِكَ أَنَّهُم مَّبْعُوثُونَ ٤ لِيَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ٥ يَوْمَ يَقُومُ النَّاسُ لِرَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ ٦﴾\nWoe to those who give less [than due], Who, when they take a measure from people, take in full. But if they give by measure or by weight to them, they cause loss. Do they not think that they will be resurrected. For a tremendous Day - The Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds?\n[Al-Mutaffifin: 1-6]\nii.) Every trade in which there is cheating is unlawful. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) has forbidden every trade which is dishonest. (See: Sahih Muslim, 1513)\nThis hadith decides the rules of trade. Any trade in which there is any form of cheating; like keeping the good fruits on top and spoilt ones at the bottom or good grains on top and bad ones at the bottom etc. A trade in which the measure of the item being traded is not known or the exact count is not known, trading in something which is not yet ready or which cannot be handed over immediately to the buyer etc. are all unlawful because there is deception in it. The buyer is not satisfied with the item being sold. Till both the buyer and the seller are fully satisfied, it remains an unlawful transaction. Only after the buyer and seller are satisfied will it become a proper trade.\niii.) No condition should be attached which nullifies the main purpose of the trade. Even if a condition is attached, the trade is lawful but the condition will not be valid. For example if the seller of a plot of land puts the condition that the buyer will not build anything on it, then the condition is invalid. In the above case, the trade is lawful but the condition will not apply. It is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“Any condition not laid down in the Book of Allah(swt) is not valid even if it is laid down a hundred times.” (See: Sahih Bukhari, 456 and Sahih Muslim, 1504)\niv.) When one person is buying a thing, it is not right if another person also tries to buy it till the first person has left it. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 2139 and Sahih Muslim, 1413)\nSome things whose trade is forbidden:\n1. Trade involving intoxicants, alcohol, dead animals, swine and idols. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 2236 and Sahih Muslim,1581). Trade involving the skin of dead animals is allowed after it has been tanned. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 5531)\n2. Trading in dogs and blood. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 2238)\n3. Earnings from prostitution and a soothsayer’s earnings are forbidden.\n4. It is unlawful to sell a free person as is narrated in a sahih hadith:\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) said, \"Allah(swt) said, 'I will be an opponent to three types of people on the Day of Resurrection: 1. One who makes a covenant in My Name, but proves treacherous; 2. One who sells a free person and eats his price; and 3. One who employs a labourer and takes full work from him but does not pay him for his labour.' \"\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 2227)\n5. Selling of surplus water is unlawful. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 2354 and Sahih Muslim, 1566)\n6. Selling the semen of a bull is haram.\n7. Selling unripe fruits while they are still on trees is haram. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 2381 and Sahih Muslim, 1536)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that fruit should not be sold until their good condition becomes evident. The fruit of date palms should not be sold until it becomes red or yellow. Dates should not be sold till they become free from all dangers of being spoilt or blighted.\nIn addition to the above, there are other trades which have been made unlawful as they are harmful to the human society. We have described only the major ones here. Moreover, trade in which both the buyer and seller are satisfied will be considered lawful as the Holy Quran says:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوَالَكُم بَيْنَكُم بِالْبَاطِلِ إِلَّا أَن تَكُونَ تِجَارَةً عَن تَرَاضٍ مِّنكُمْ\nO you who have believed, do not consume one another's wealth unjustly but only [in lawful] business by mutual consent.\n[An-Nisa: 29]\nThis is the most important principle of trade in Islam. That is why a transaction in which both the seller and the buyer are not satisfied is haram."],[333,"§Traitor\nSee ‘Betrayal’."],[334,"§Traveller\nSee ‘Hospitality’."],[335,"§Tubba\n‘Tubba’ is described twice in the Holy Quran:\n﴿أَهُمْ خَيْرٌ أَمْ قَوْمُ تُبَّعٍ وَالَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِهِمْ ۚ أَهْلَكْنَاهُمْ ۖ إِنَّهُمْ كَانُوا مُجْرِمِينَ ٣٧﴾\nAre they better or the people of Tubba' and those before them? We destroyed them, [for] indeed, they were criminals.\n[Ad-Dukhan: 37]\n﴿كَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوحٍ وَأَصْحَابُ الرَّسِّ وَثَمُودُ ١٢ وَعَادٌ وَفِرْعَوْنُ وَإِخْوَانُ لُوطٍ ١٣ وَأَصْحَابُ الْأَيْكَةِ وَقَوْمُ تُبَّعٍ ۚ كُلٌّ كَذَّبَ الرُّسُلَ فَحَقَّ وَعِيدِ ١٤﴾\nThe people of Noah denied before them, and the companions of the well and Thamud. And 'Aad and Pharaoh and the brothers of Lot. And the companions of the thicket and the people of Tubba'. All denied the messengers, so My threat was justly fulfilled.\n[Qaf: 12-14]\n‘Tubba’ is the royal title of the kings of Himyar in Yemen who ruled for one and a half century around 1 A. D. Just as the Egyptian kings were titled ‘Pharaoh’, they were titled ‘Tubba’.\nSome scholars are of the opinion that this was the name of a pious man who invited people towards ‘monotheism’. But like the other tribes, even his tribe rejected him and as a result they were punished severely.\nAisha(ra) also said that he was a holy man and hence should not be cursed.\n‘Ka’b’ who was a companion of the Holy Prophet(saws) said that Allah(swt) did not call ‘Tubba’ evil but called his tribe evil. It is in fact narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Do not curse Tubba because he had become a Muslim.” (See: Musnad Ahmad, 22880)\nThis hadith is ‘Zaeef’ because one narrator ‘Abdullah bin Lahiya’ is ‘Zaeef’. But it is corroborated by other Mursal hadith.\nFrom the verses of the Surah-Qaf we get the impression of a prophet as prophets were sent to all the tribes mentioned in them and these tribes rejected their prophets. These prophets have been clearly described in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith, but nowhere does it say that ‘Tubba’ was a prophet. Therefore we cannot consider ‘Tubba’ to be a prophet."],[336,"§Tuwa\n‘Tuwa’ has been described in two places in the Holy Quran and in both the places Allah(swt) commands Musa(as) to remove his footwear as he is in the sacred ground of ‘Tuwa’ and listen carefully to what Allah(swt) instructs:\n﴿إِنِّي أَنَا رَبُّكَ فَاخْلَعْ نَعْلَيْكَ ۖ إِنَّكَ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًى ١٢ وَأَنَا اخْتَرْتُكَ فَاسْتَمِعْ لِمَا يُوحَىٰ ١٣﴾\nIndeed, I am your Lord, so remove your sandals. Indeed, you are in the sacred valley of Tuwa. And I have chosen you, so listen to what is revealed [to you].\n[Surah 20: 12, 13]\nAt another place Allah(swt) commands:\n﴿هَلْ أَتَاكَ حَدِيثُ مُوسَىٰ ١٥ إِذْ نَادَاهُ رَبُّهُ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًى ١٦ اذْهَبْ إِلَىٰ فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّهُ طَغَىٰ ١٧﴾\nHas there reached you the story of Moses? When his Lord called to him in the sacred valley of Tuwa,\"Go to Pharaoh. Indeed, he has transgressed.\n[An-Nazi’at: 15-17]\nThis event took place when Musa(as) was coming back from Madyan to Egypt with his wife and children. There he was given the good news that he was being made a prophet by Allah(swt) and then he is commanded to go to the Pharaoh. The Pharaoh had become very arrogant and a tyrant. Musa(as) was commanded to first give him the message of ‘Tawheed’ and then free the Bani-Israel from his evil rule.\nWhat is this ground of ‘Tuwa’? We come to know from the Holy Quran that it is in the valley of Mount ‘Tur’:\n﴿فَلَمَّا قَضَىٰ مُوسَى الْأَجَلَ وَسَارَ بِأَهْلِهِ آنَسَ مِن جَانِبِ الطُّورِ نَارًا قَالَ لِأَهْلِهِ امْكُثُوا إِنِّي آنَسْتُ نَارًا لَّعَلِّي آتِيكُم مِّنْهَا بِخَبَرٍ أَوْ جَذْوَةٍ مِّنَ النَّارِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَصْطَلُونَ ٢٩ فَلَمَّا أَتَاهَا نُودِيَ مِن شَاطِئِ الْوَادِ الْأَيْمَنِ فِي الْبُقْعَةِ الْمُبَارَكَةِ مِنَ الشَّجَرَةِ أَن يَا مُوسَىٰ إِنِّي أَنَا اللَّـهُ رَبُّ الْعَالَمِينَ ٣٠﴾\nAnd when Moses had completed the term and was traveling with his family, he perceived from the direction of the mount a fire. He said to his family, \"Stay here; indeed, I have perceived a fire. Perhaps I will bring you from there [some] information or burning wood from the fire that you may warm yourselves.\" But when he came to it, he was called from the right side of the valley in a blessed spot - from the tree, \"O Moses, indeed I am Allah, Lord of the worlds.\"\n[Al-Qasas: 29, 30]\n(For more information see: ‘Musa(as)’)"],[337,"§Uff\n‘Uff’ is an Arabic word used to express displeasure, hurt or some grief and it is used in the Holy Quran in connection with the behaviour towards one’s parents:\n﴿وَقَضَىٰ رَبُّكَ أَلَّا تَعْبُدُوا إِلَّا إِيَّاهُ وَبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ إِحْسَانًا ۚ إِمَّا يَبْلُغَنَّ عِندَكَ الْكِبَرَ أَحَدُهُمَا أَوْ كِلَاهُمَا فَلَا تَقُل لَّهُمَا أُفٍّ وَلَا تَنْهَرْهُمَا وَقُل لَّهُمَا قَوْلًا كَرِيمًا ٢٣﴾\nThy Lord hath decreed that ye worship none but Him, and that ye be kind to parents. Whether one or both of them attain old age in thy life, say not to them a word of contempt, nor repel them, but address them in terms of honour.\n[Bani-Israel: 23]\nIn this verse, by forbidding the use of this contempt expressing word for one’s parents, the Holy Quran is warning us that when we cannot use a mere word against them, we obviously cannot hurt them in any way whatsoever. From this we can definitely say that a book in which so much importance is given to one’s parents can only be the best among all the books of this world."],[338,"§Uhud\nThis is the name of a mountain in Madina. In its valley a great war was fought which is known as the ‘Battle of Uhud’. To avenge the defeat at the hands of the Muslims in the battle of Badr, the disbelievers gathered a large army from the places surrounding Makka. This army consisted of three thousand men, two hundred of which were cavalry (Ibn-Hisham:3:62). In 3 A. H., they started making preparations to attack Madina. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came to know of it, he consulted the other Muslims as to whether they should stay in Madina and protect themselves or come out of the city and face the enemy. The majority were in favour of coming out of Madina and facing the enemy. Accepting their decision, the Holy Prophet(saws) went into his house and came out wearing his warrior robes though he himself was in favour of staying back in Madina and fighting the enemy. This is one instance of his exemplary character. Some of his companions, including his paternal uncle Hamza wanted him to implement his decision. But the Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “Once a prophet dons the war robes, he does not remove them till the war is over.” (Tabri, 7: 372)\nIn this way, the Holy Prophet(saws) set out from Madina to Uhud with an army of one thousand. On the way the leader of the hypocrites, Abdullah-bin-Ubaiyy went back to Madina with one third of the army. This discouraged many of the remaining soldiers and even a few true Muslims started thinking of going back. But they continued on their way and finally met the enemy in the valley of Uhud.\nThe Muslim army reached a place where the Uhud mountain was behind them and Madina was in front of them. The Holy Prophet(saws) stationed a group of fifty archers on a mountain in front of the Uhud mountain to prevent the enemy from attacking the Muslim army from behind. The archers were given strict instructions that they should not leave their posts even though the Muslims won the war. This mountain is called the Jabl-e-Rumat meaning the mountain of the archer soldiers.\nThe war started. The enemy was defeated and Muslims won. Twenty-two enemy soldiers were killed. When the archers stationed on the mountain saw that the Muslims had won and were collecting the spoils of war, even they left their posts and started collecting the booty in spite of their leader Abdullah-bin-Zubair pleading not to do it as it was against the Holy Prophet’s(saws) orders. But they did not listen to him and said,” But we have won the war.”\nWhat the Holy Prophet(saws) had predicted happened. Khalid-bin-Waleed, who had not yet embraced Islam, rounded the Uhud mountain with a small group of soldiers and attacked the Muslims who were busily collecting the war booty. The archers who were supposed to prevent this attack had reached the plain ground and a couple of them who had stayed back could not prevent the attack.\nNow the situation was that the enemy was attacking from behind and the Muslims were trapped in the valley and could not protect themselves. Seventy sahaba (companions) were martyred. Among them was the Holy Prophet’s(saws) uncle Hamza. Even the Holy Prophet(saws) was injured and lost a couple of teeth.\nThen, Allah(swt)’s help arrived in that the enemy even after winning the war went back to Makka as they did not dare to enter Madina and Madina, the center of Islam was saved from being destroyed.\nIn the Holy Quran, this war is not mentioned as the battle of Uhud, but the verses of Aal-i-Imran were revealed in this connection.\n﴿وَإِذْ غَدَوْتَ مِنْ أَهْلِكَ تُبَوِّئُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ مَقَاعِدَ لِلْقِتَالِ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ ١٢١﴾\nRemember that morning Thou didst leave Thy household (early) to post the faithful at their stations for battle: And Allah heareth and knoweth all things.\n[Aal-i-Imran: 121]\nThe battle described here is the battle of Uhud.\n﴿إِذْ هَمَّت طَّائِفَتَانِ مِنكُمْ أَن تَفْشَلَا وَاللَّـهُ وَلِيُّهُمَا ۗ وَعَلَى اللَّـهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ ١٢٢﴾\nRemember two of your parties Meditated cowardice; but Allah was their protector, and in Allah should the faithful (Ever) put their trust.\n[Aal-i-Imran: 122]\nThese two groups as narrated in Sahih Bukhari (4558) and Sahih Muslim (1949) were Banu-Haarisa and Banu-Salma which were discouraged when Abdullah-bin-Ubaiyy-bin-Salool deserted them.\n﴿وَلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّـهُ بِبَدْرٍ وَأَنتُمْ أَذِلَّةٌ ۖ فَاتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ ١٢٣﴾\nAllah had helped you at Badr, when ye were a contemptible little force; then fear Allah; thus May ye show your gratitude.\n[Aal-i-Imran: 123]\nThis battle of Badr took place in 2 A. H 11 March, 624 A. D in which the Muslims had triumphed. In retaliation, exactly one year later the disbelievers attacked Madina and this is known as the battle of Uhud.\n﴿إِذْ تَقُولُ لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَلَن يَكْفِيَكُمْ أَن يُمِدَّكُمْ رَبُّكُم بِثَلَاثَةِ آلَافٍ مِّنَ الْمَلَائِكَةِ مُنزَلِينَ ١٢٤ بَلَىٰ ۚ إِن تَصْبِرُوا وَتَتَّقُوا وَيَأْتُوكُم مِّن فَوْرِهِمْ هَـٰذَا يُمْدِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُم بِخَمْسَةِ آلَافٍ مِّنَ الْمَلَائِكَةِ مُسَوِّمِينَ ١٢٥ وَمَا جَعَلَهُ اللَّـهُ إِلَّا بُشْرَىٰ لَكُمْ وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ قُلُوبُكُم بِهِ ۗ وَمَا النَّصْرُ إِلَّا مِنْ عِندِ اللَّـهِ الْعَزِيزِ الْحَكِيمِ ١٢٦﴾\nRemember thou saidst to the Faithful: \"Is it not enough for you that Allah should help you with three thousand angels (Specially) sent down? \"Yea, - if ye remain firm, and act aright, even if the enemy should rush here on you in hot haste, your Lord would help you with five thousand angels Making a terrific onslaught. Allah made it but a message of hope for you, and an assurance to your hearts: (in any case) there is no help except from Allah. The Exalted, the Wise.\n[Aal-i-Imran: 124-126]\nThe reason why Allah(swt) did not help the Muslims with these three thousand and five thousand angels in the battle of Uhud was not because the Muslims were not brave or disobeyed the Holy Prophet(saws) but because they were overtaken with greed and got busy collecting the war booty. The Holy Quran is admonishing them saying that if they had not done so, Allah(swt) would have not only helped them with three thousand but five thousand angels. The method of help would be that these angels instead of fighting for them would strengthen the hearts of the Muslims and strike terror in the hearts of the enemy so that the Muslims could easily triumph.\nلِيَقْطَعَ طَرَفًا مِّنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أَوْ يَكْبِتَهُمْ فَيَنقَلِبُوا خَائِبِينَ\nThat He might cut off a fringe of the Unbelievers or expose them to infamy, and they should then be turned back, frustrated of their purpose.\n[Aal-i-Imran: 127]\nAnd that is how it happened. One, the Muslims won the war and killed a group of the disbelievers. Second, the disbelievers were humiliated and went back because they had come with the intention of destroying Madina and wiping out Islam but they could not do so. Even though no soldiers were stationed in Madina, they lacked the courage to enter it and were thus unsuccessful in their main aim.\nAs was previously mentioned, a few teeth of the Holy Prophet(saws) were also martyred and blood was flowing from his face. In this state he supplicated:\n“How can that tribe be successful, who have hurt their prophet.”\n(Sahih Muslim 1791)\nThen Allah(swt) revealed the following verses:\n﴿لَيْسَ لَكَ مِنَ الْأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ أَوْ يَتُوبَ عَلَيْهِمْ أَوْ يُعَذِّبَهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ ظَالِمُونَ ١٢٨ وَلِلَّـهِ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ ۚ يَغْفِرُ لِمَن يَشَاءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَن يَشَاءُ ۚ وَاللَّـهُ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ١٢٩﴾\nNot for thee, (but for Allah), is the decision: Whether He turn in mercy to them, or punish them; for they are indeed wrong-doers. To Allah belongeth all that is in the heavens and on earth. He forgiveth whom He pleaseth and punisheth whom He pleaseth; but Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.\n[Aal-i-Imran: 128-129]\nAnd this word of Allah(swt) came true because these opponents of Islam later embraced Islam and became the protectors of Islam. Through them Islam spread to other parts of the world. The same Khalid-bin-Waleed who rounded the Uhud mountain and attacked the Muslims, was favoured by Allah(swt) and accomplished so many successful missions that even today it astounds many renowned army chiefs."],[339,"§Ummi\nIn two verses of the surah A’raaf, the Holy Prophet(saws) has been called ‘ummi’:\n﴿الَّذِينَ يَتَّبِعُونَ الرَّسُولَ النَّبِيَّ الْأُمِّيَّ الَّذِي يَجِدُونَهُ مَكْتُوبًا عِندَهُمْ فِي التَّوْرَاةِ وَالْإِنجِيلِ يَأْمُرُهُم بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَيَنْهَاهُمْ عَنِ الْمُنكَرِ وَيُحِلُّ لَهُمُ الطَّيِّبَاتِ وَيُحَرِّمُ عَلَيْهِمُ الْخَبَائِثَ وَيَضَعُ عَنْهُمْ إِصْرَهُمْ وَالْأَغْلَالَ الَّتِي كَانَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ فَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بِهِ وَعَزَّرُوهُ وَنَصَرُوهُ وَاتَّبَعُوا النُّورَ الَّذِي أُنزِلَ مَعَهُ ۙ أُولَـٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ ١٥٧ قُلْ يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ إِنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّـهِ إِلَيْكُمْ جَمِيعًا الَّذِي لَهُ مُلْكُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۖ لَا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ ۖ فَآمِنُوا بِاللَّـهِ وَرَسُولِهِ النَّبِيِّ الْأُمِّيِّ الَّذِي يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّـهِ وَكَلِمَاتِهِ وَاتَّبِعُوهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ ١٥٨﴾\n\"Those who follow the messenger, the unlettered Prophet, whom they find mentioned in their own (scriptures),- in the law and the Gospel;- for he commands them what is just and forbids them what is evil; he allows them as lawful what is good (and pure) and prohibits them from what is bad (and impure); He releases them from their heavy burdens and from the yokes that are upon them. So it is those who believe in him, honour him, help him, and follow the light which is sent down with him,- it is they who will prosper.\" Say: \"O men! I am sent unto you all, as the Messenger of Allah, to Whom belongeth the dominion of the heavens and the earth: there is no god but He: it is He That giveth both life and death. So believe in Allah and His Messenger, the Unlettered Prophet, who believeth in Allah and His words: follow him that (so) ye may be guided.\"\n[Al-A’raaf: 157-158]\nMost of the scholars say that the meaning of ‘ummi’ is ‘unlettered’. While we cannot say that this is wrong, it is necessary to know the real meaning of the word. This is the translation of the Hebrew word ‘goyim’ whose plural is ‘umam’. The Jews called all the others ‘umum’. In their religious scriptures, these non-Jews had no rights at all and were considered as equal to animals. So much so that when the Jews took or rather snatched something from them, they considered it a sin to even return it. This attitude has been severely criticised in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَمِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ مَنْ إِن تَأْمَنْهُ بِقِنطَارٍ يُؤَدِّهِ إِلَيْكَ وَمِنْهُم مَّنْ إِن تَأْمَنْهُ بِدِينَارٍ لَّا يُؤَدِّهِ إِلَيْكَ إِلَّا مَا دُمْتَ عَلَيْهِ قَائِمًا ۗ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قَالُوا لَيْسَ عَلَيْنَا فِي الْأُمِّيِّينَ سَبِيلٌ وَيَقُولُونَ عَلَى اللَّـهِ الْكَذِبَ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ ٧٥ بَلَىٰ مَنْ أَوْفَىٰ بِعَهْدِهِ وَاتَّقَىٰ فَإِنَّ اللَّـهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِينَ ٧٦﴾\nAmong the People of the Book are some who, if entrusted with a hoard of gold, will (readily) pay it back; others, who, if entrusted with a single silver coin, will not repay it unless thou constantly stoodest demanding, because, they say, \"there is no call on us (to keep faith) with these ignorant (Pagans).\" but they tell a lie against Allah, and (well) they know it. Nay.- Those that keep their plighted faith and act aright,-verily Allah loves those who act aright.\n[Aal-i-Imran: 75-76]\nAccording to the Holy Quran, all men are the creatures of Allah(swt) and the best are those who steadfastly obey His orders:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ إِنَّا خَلَقْنَاكُم مِّن ذَكَرٍ وَأُنثَىٰ وَجَعَلْنَاكُمْ شُعُوبًا وَقَبَائِلَ لِتَعَارَفُوا ۚ إِنَّ أَكْرَمَكُمْ عِندَ اللَّـهِ أَتْقَاكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ عَلِيمٌ خَبِيرٌ ١٣﴾\nO mankind! We created you from a single (pair) of a male and a female, and made you into nations and tribes, that ye may know each other (not that ye may despise (each other). Verily the most honoured of you in the sight of Allah is (he who is) the most righteous of you. And Allah has full knowledge and is well acquainted (with all things).\n[Al-Hujuraat: 13]\nThe Jews believed in the doctrine that messengers and prophets would come only from the tribe of Bani-Israel and from no other tribe and they believed that especially from the Arab tribe which was from the family of Ismael(as), no prophet would come.\nDisproving this belief of the Jews, Allah(swt) says that He(swt) has made ‘ummi’ a prophet; that is somebody who was not from Bani-Israel.\nAt one place in the Holy Quran, it is explained clearly:\n﴿هُوَ الَّذِي بَعَثَ فِي الْأُمِّيِّينَ رَسُولًا مِّنْهُمْ يَتْلُو عَلَيْهِمْ آيَاتِهِ وَيُزَكِّيهِمْ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتَابَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَإِن كَانُوا مِن قَبْلُ لَفِي ضَلَالٍ مُّبِينٍ ٢﴾\nIt is He Who has sent amongst the Unlettered a messenger from among themselves, to rehearse to them His Signs, to sanctify them, and to instruct them in Scripture and Wisdom,- although they had been, before, in manifest error.\n[Al-Jumu’a: 2]\nHere not only the Holy Prophet(saws), but the whole Arab tribe has been called ‘ummi’.\nIn the Bible, they have been called the other tribe. (See: Yeshayah, 49-6)\nThus, it is clear that ‘ummi’ does not mean ‘unlettered’ but the non-Jewish tribes. Because the Jews had the divine books and considered themselves the guardians and followers of those books, the people who did not possess these books came to be called ‘unlettered’ as is meant in surah-Baqara:\n﴿وَمِنْهُمْ أُمِّيُّونَ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ الْكِتَابَ إِلَّا أَمَانِيَّ وَإِنْ هُمْ إِلَّا يَظُنُّونَ ٧٨﴾\nAnd there are among them illiterates, who know not the Book, but (see therein their own) desires, and they do nothing but conjecture.\n[Al-Baqara: 78]\nIn the above verse, the word ‘Ummiyun’ which is the plural of ‘ummi’ is used in the sense of ‘illiterate’ and the people meant are the illiterate Jews who lived their lives based on their whims and conjectures that they were the chosen ones of Allah(swt) and would never go to hell and even if they did, it would only be for a few days after which their ancestors would save them etc."],[340,"§Ummul-Qura\nThis is the name given to Makka which means, the central city, or the main city etc. Every central or nodal thing in Arabic is called ‘Umm’. For example Lauhe-Mahfooz is called ‘Ummul-Kitab’ because it is the main book of all the celestial books. Similarly surah Fateha is called ‘Ummul-Quran’ because it is the gist and core of the Holy Quran.\nIn the Holy Quran, the word ‘Ummul-Qura’ occurs twice. In both instances, the city meant is Makka. First it occurs in surah Al-An’aam:\nوَهَٰذَا كِتَابٌ أَنزَلْنَاهُ مُبَارَكٌ مُّصَدِّقُ الَّذِي بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَلِتُنذِرَ أُمَّ الْقُرَىٰ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهَا\nAnd this is a Book which We have sent down, bringing blessings, and confirming (the revelations) which came before it: that thou mayest warn the mother of cities and all around her.\n[Al-An’aam: 92]\nSecond, it occurs in surah Ash-Shura:\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْكَ قُرْآنًا عَرَبِيًّا لِّتُنذِرَ أُمَّ الْقُرَىٰ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهَا\nThus have We sent by inspiration to thee an Arabic Qur'an: that thou mayest warn the Mother of Cities and all around her.\n[Ash-Shura: 7]\nBy instructing the people of Ummul-Qura, Allah(swt) has in fact instructed the whole mankind, as it says in surah Al-A’raaf:\nقُلْ يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ إِنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ إِلَيْكُمْ جَمِيعًا الَّذِي لَهُ مُلْكُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۖ لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ ۖ\nSay: \"O men! I am sent unto you all, as the Messenger of Allah, to Whom belongeth the dominion of the heavens and the earth: there is no god but He: it is He That giveth both life and death.\n[Al-A’raaf: 158]\nIt says in surah Al-An’aam:\nوَأُوحِيَ إِلَيَّ هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنُ لِأُنذِرَكُم بِهِ وَمَن بَلَغَ ۚ\nThis Qur'an hath been revealed to me by inspiration, that I may warn you and all whom it reaches.\n[Al-An’aam: 19]\nIt says in surah Al-Furqan:\n﴿تَبَارَكَ الَّذِي نَزَّلَ الْفُرْقَانَ عَلَىٰ عَبْدِهِ لِيَكُونَ لِلْعَالَمِينَ نَذِيرًا ١﴾\nBlessed is He who sent down the criterion to His servant, that it may be an admonition to all creatures.\n[Al-Furqan: 1]\nIn the above verse, the Quran is called the Furqan because it clearly distinguishes between truth and falsehood.\nIt is narrated in one Sahih Hadith that whereas all the prophets were sent to a particular tribe, I (Muhammad saws) was sent for the entire mankind."],[341,"§Umra\nUmra is also a form of Ibadat or worship which is done after going to Makka.\nوَأَتِمُّوا الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ لِلَّـهِ\nAnd complete the Hajj or 'umra in the service of Allah.\n[Al-Baqara: 196]\nIn the light of the above verse, some scholars say that it is obligatory at least once in a lifetime just like the Haj; but most of the scholars do not think so.\nUmra can be performed at any time during the whole year. The method is that a person makes the intention to perform umra, wears the ihraam at the meeqat and upon reaching Makka circumambulates the Kaaba seven times, offers two rakat nafl salah at the Maqaam-e-Ibraheem (or at any other place in the haram), completes seven rounds between Safa and Marwa and then either completely shaves his head (halaq which is preferable) or shortens the hair with the help of a pair of scissors (Qasr). In case of women, they should cut a part from the end of their braids. Then, they can have a bath and wear normal clothes and their umra is complete.\nAll the things forbidden during the Haj are also forbidden during umra. For detailed information see ‘Hajj’.\nUmra during Ramadan:\nUmra performed during the month of Ramadan has great rewards and according to a Sahih Hadith is equal in importance and benefits to Haj."],[342,"§Urjoon\nUrjoon means a date stalk. In the Holy Quran the moon has been described and it says that Allah(swt) has measured mansions for it and traversing them, the moon begins to look like the dried up lower part of the date-stalk. (See: Quran, Surah-36, Yaseen, Verse-39)\nAllah(swt) is actually telling us that He(swt) is All-Powerful and whatever is happening in this universe is according to His wish and will. In the preceding verse, the sun is being described which is moving in its own orbit. In these verses, the sun-worshippers and moon-worshippers are being warned that the sun and moon are nothing but cosmic entities created by Allah(swt) and which are moving according to the will of their Lord and should not be worshipped in any form. Allah(swt) alone has the right to be worshipped. This has been explained excellently in the Holy Quran in the words of Ibraheem(as):\n﴿فَلَمَّا جَنَّ عَلَيْهِ اللَّيْلُ رَأَىٰ كَوْكَبًا ۖ قَالَ هَٰذَا رَبِّي ۖ فَلَمَّا أَفَلَ قَالَ لَا أُحِبُّ الْآفِلِينَ ٧٦ فَلَمَّا رَأَى الْقَمَرَ بَازِغًا قَالَ هَٰذَا رَبِّي ۖ فَلَمَّا أَفَلَ قَالَ لَئِن لَّمْ يَهْدِنِي رَبِّي لَأَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الضَّالِّينَ ٧٧ فَلَمَّا رَأَى الشَّمْسَ بَازِغَةً قَالَ هَٰذَا رَبِّي هَٰذَا أَكْبَرُ ۖ فَلَمَّا أَفَلَتْ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ إِنِّي بَرِيءٌ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُونَ ٧٨ إِنِّي وَجَّهْتُ وَجْهِيَ لِلَّذِي فَطَرَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ حَنِيفًا ۖ وَمَا أَنَا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ ٧٩ وَحَاجَّهُ قَوْمُهُ ۚ قَالَ أَتُحَاجُّونِّي فِي اللَّهِ وَقَدْ هَدَانِ ۚ وَلَا أَخَافُ مَا تُشْرِكُونَ بِهِ إِلَّا أَن يَشَاءَ رَبِّي شَيْئًا ۗ وَسِعَ رَبِّي كُلَّ شَيْءٍ عِلْمًا ۗ أَفَلَا تَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٨٠﴾\nWhen the night covered him over, He saw a star: He said: \"This is my Lord.\" But when it set, He said: \"I love not those that set.\" When he saw the moon rising in splendour, he said: \"This is my Lord.\" But when the moon set, He said: \"unless my Lord guide me, I shall surely be among those who go astray.\" When he saw the sun rising in splendour, he said: \"This is my Lord; this is the greatest (of all).\" But when the sun set, he said: \"O my people! I am indeed free from your (guilt) of giving partners to Allah. \"For me, I have set my face, firmly and truly, towards Him Who created the heavens and the earth, and never shall I give partners to Allah.\" His people disputed with him. He said: \" (Come) ye to dispute with me, about Allah, when He (Himself) hath guided me? I fear not (the beings) ye associate with Allah: Unless my Lord willeth, (nothing can happen). My Lord comprehendeth in His knowledge all things. Will ye not (yourselves) be admonished?\n[Al-An’aam: 76-80]"],[343,"§Uzair\nA person named ‘Uzair’ is described at one place in the Holy Quran, whom the Jews considered as the son of Allah(swt) (Inna Aoozubillah):\n﴿وَقَالَتِ الْيَهُودُ عُزَيْرٌ ابْنُ اللَّـهِ وَقَالَتِ النَّصَارَى الْمَسِيحُ ابْنُ اللَّـهِ ۖ ذَٰلِكَ قَوْلُهُم بِأَفْوَاهِهِمْ ۖ يُضَاهِئُونَ قَوْلَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِن قَبْلُ ۚ قَاتَلَهُمُ اللَّـهُ ۚ أَنَّىٰ يُؤْفَكُونَ ٣٠﴾\nThe Jews call 'Uzair a son of Allah, and the Christians call Christ the son of Allah. That is a saying from their mouth; (in this) they but imitate what the unbelievers of old used to say. Allah's curse be on them: how they are deluded away from the Truth!\n[At-Tawba: 30]\nThat is, there is a strong connection between the Jews calling Uzair the son of Allah(swt) and the Christians calling Isa(as) the son of Allah(swt).\nWhat happened was that after Sulaiman(as), idol-worship spread among the Jews. Then, BukhtNasar, the king of Babylon attacked Palestine and the Baitul-Maqdas was destroyed. All the copies of the Taurah kept there were destroyed and thousands of Jews were captured and taken away to Babylon. They were held prisoners for seventy years and were finally freed in the fifth century B. C. A man named ‘Uzair’ claimed that he had rewritten the Taurah and started teaching it. All the Jews started gathering around him and considered him their greatest leader after Musa(as) as he had rewritten their Taurah. One other thing which he did was to separate the children of non-Jewish women who had married Jewish men, so that there was no non-Jewish strain in the Jewish people. Due to these things, some people started considering him as a form of God and the son of God and seeing this the Christians also started calling Isa(as) as the son of God(Inna Aoozu Billah).\nThe Jews who called Uzair the son of God were also present in Madina. So, when this verse was revealed they did not pay any heed to it and started questioning as to how they could embrace a religion which does not believe that Uzair was the son of God when all their forefathers had believed it because Uzair was instrumental in rewriting their holy Taurah. They believed that but for the efforts of Uzair, Judaism would have been wiped out from the face of the earth and thus he was the son of God.\nEven if today the Jews do not consider Uzair the son of God, this verse of the Holy Quran is still relevant because it was basically addressed to the Jews of those days. Similarly there were quite a few Christians who did not consider Isa(as) the son of God. The Egyptian padre Aryanoes of the third century A. D. and his followers did not consider Isa(as) to be the son of God and even today there are many people who do not think so."],[344,"§Uzza\nIn the surah 53, An-Najm of the Holy Quran, the names of three deities have been mentioned and Uzza is one of them. Uzza is derived from the word ‘Aziz’ which is one of the attributes of Allah(swt). Uzza was the idol of the tribe of Banu-Ghatfan and was placed under a tree in the valley of Naqla which was between Makka and Taif. Behind this there was a valley in which was discarded the blood of the sacrificial animals. Then slowly the worship of this idol spread to Yemen. Once, the king of Hira, Munzir offered four hundred war bounties to this deity. By and by even the people of Quraish started worshipping this idol; so much so that even while circumambulating the Kaaba they would call out to it and took pride in worshipping it.\nThat is the reason why Abu-Sufyan, the chieftain of Makka during the war of Uhud would give the war-cry “Our goddess Uzza will help us and O Muslims! You have no Uzza” Upon hearing this the Holy Prophet(saws) told the Muslims:\n“Say, our Protector is Allah(swt), you have no protector.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 5393)"],[345,"§Wahi\n‘Wahi’ means secret message because in this state it is not compulsory to see the one who gives the message and in fact other than the person to whom the message is revealed, no one else should see the one who delivers the message. Only the effect of the revelation can be seen. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that Aisha(ra) said:\n“Verily even on a cold day, when the Holy Prophet(saws) received Divine inspiration (revelation), I saw sweat on his forehead.” (Sahih Bukhari, 2 and Sahih Muslim,2333)\nIn the Holy Quran, three forms of revelations are described:\n﴿وَمَا كَانَ لِبَشَرٍ أَن يُكَلِّمَهُ اللَّـهُ إِلَّا وَحْيًا أَوْ مِن وَرَاءِ حِجَابٍ أَوْ يُرْسِلَ رَسُولًا فَيُوحِيَ بِإِذْنِهِ مَا يَشَاءُ ۚ إِنَّهُ عَلِيٌّ حَكِيمٌ ٥١﴾\nAnd it is not for any human being that Allah should speak to him except by revelation or from behind a partition or that He sends a messenger to reveal, by His permission, what He wills. Indeed, He is Most High and Wise.\n[Ash-Shura: 51]\nThe first type of revelation is that Allah(swt) puts something in the heart of the prophet or shows it to him in a dream as the dreams of prophets are always true. That is why Ibraheem(as) made his only son Ismael(as) lie down on the ground to sacrifice him for Allah(swt) because he had seen the same thing in his dream. But for people other than the prophets it is not right to act according to their dreams.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) says about the first revelation which he received:\n“Whatever I see in the night in my dream, I find it coming true in the morning.”\n(See: Sahih Bukhari,3)\nThe second type of revelation is one in which Allah(swt) Himself speaks from behind a curtain and commands the prophet or gives him instructions as in the case of Musa(as) due to which Musa(as) became impatient and insisted on seeing Allah(swt). Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَلَمَّا جَاءَ مُوسَىٰ لِمِيقَاتِنَا وَكَلَّمَهُ رَبُّهُ قَالَ رَبِّ أَرِنِي أَنظُرْ إِلَيْكَ ۚ قَالَ لَن تَرَانِي وَلَـٰكِنِ انظُرْ إِلَى الْجَبَلِ فَإِنِ اسْتَقَرَّ مَكَانَهُ فَسَوْفَ تَرَانِي ۚ فَلَمَّا تَجَلَّىٰ رَبُّهُ لِلْجَبَلِ جَعَلَهُ دَكًّا وَخَرَّ مُوسَىٰ صَعِقًا ۚ فَلَمَّا أَفَاقَ قَالَ سُبْحَانَكَ تُبْتُ إِلَيْكَ وَأَنَا أَوَّلُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ١٤٣﴾\nAnd when Moses arrived at Our appointed time and his Lord spoke to him, he said, \"My Lord, show me [Yourself] that I may look at You.\" [Allah] said, \"You will not see Me, but look at the mountain; if it should remain in place, then you will see Me.\" But when his Lord appeared to the mountain, He rendered it level, and Moses fell unconscious. And when he awoke, he said, \"Exalted are You! I have repented to You, and I am the first of the believers.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 143]\nThe third type of revelation is that in which Jibrail(as) or some other angel brought the message from Allah(swt) to the prophet.\nThe Holy Quran was revealed using the third type of revelation; that is Jibrail(as) brought the messages to the Holy Prophet(saws). The first revelation was given to the Holy Prophet(saws) when he was worshipping Allah(swt) in the cave of Hira. An angel came up to him and said, “Read!”. The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “I cannot read.” Jibrail(as) pressed him hard and let go of him and said,”Read!” The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “I cannot read.” The angel pressed him hard a second time and then let go of him. This happened three times. Then the angel recited the following verse of the Holy Quran:\n﴿اقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ ١ خَلَقَ الْإِنسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ ٢ اقْرَأْ وَرَبُّكَ الْأَكْرَمُ ٣ الَّذِي عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِ ٤ عَلَّمَ الْإِنسَانَ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْ ٥﴾\nRecite in the name of your Lord who created - Created man from a clinging substance. Recite, and your Lord is the most Generous - Who taught by the pen - Taught man that which he knew not.\n[Al-Alaq: 1-5] (See: Sahih Bukhari,3 and Sahih Muslim,160)\nThis was the first revelation conveyed by Jibrail(as) to the Holy Prophet(saws).\nOne day when the Holy Prophet(saws) was going somewhere, he(saws) heard a voice from the sky. When he(saws) looked up he(saws) saw that it was the same angel who had come to him in the cave Hira, but that day he was in his original form. He was seated in a chair which spanned the earth and the sky. After this, whenever there was a revelation, the Holy Prophet(saws) would start moving his lips fast so as to remember everything. The following verse was revealed in this connection:\n﴿لَا تُحَرِّكْ بِهِ لِسَانَكَ لِتَعْجَلَ بِهِ ١٦ إِنَّ عَلَيْنَا جَمْعَهُ وَقُرْآنَهُ ١٧ فَإِذَا قَرَأْنَاهُ فَاتَّبِعْ قُرْآنَهُ ١٨﴾\nMove not your tongue with it, [O Muhammad], to hasten with recitation of the Qur'an. Indeed, upon Us is its collection [in your heart] and [to make possible] its recitation. So when We have recited it [through Gabriel], then follow its recitation.\n[Al-Qiyama: 16-18]\nWhen the angel came with the verses from the Holy Quran, the Holy Prophet(saws) would start reading them along with Jibrail(as) so as to remember everything. When Allah(swt) saw this He(swt) gave the Holy Prophet(saws) the good news that He(swt) would ensure that everything gets imprinted in his heart. In this way the Holy Quran was revealed over a period of twenty-three years and was imprinted in his heart. Therefore the Holy Prophet(saws) never had to memorize the Holy Quran as we all need to do. Then, the Holy Prophet(saws) would make his companions write it down."],[346,"§Wali\n‘Wali’ means a ‘Protector’. In the Holy Quran, ‘Wali’ is one of the Most Beautiful names of Allah(swt). The Holy Quran warns again and again that the people who invoke others instead of Allah(swt), worship them and seek their help will not find any protector as Allah(swt) is the ‘Protector’ only of those people who believe in His Oneness and realize that only Allah(swt) is the Creator and Protector of everything:\nوَمَن يُضْلِلِ اللَّهُ فَمَا لَهُ مِن وَلِيٍّ مِّن بَعْدِهِ ۗ\nAnd he whom Allah sends astray - for him there is no protector beyond Him.\n[Ash-Shura: 44]\nThe word ‘wali’ has also been used for the slaves of Allah(swt). The plural form is ‘Aulia’. Two types of ‘Aulia’ have been described in the Holy Quran:\n1. One is ‘Aulia-e-Satan’, that is the friends of the Satan whose main task is to try to mislead the people and plot against Islam. The Holy Quran says about them:\nإِنَّا جَعَلْنَا الشَّيَاطِينَ أَوْلِيَاءَ لِلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ\nIndeed, We have made the devils allies to those who do not believe.\n[Al-A’raf: 27]\nإِنَّهُمُ اتَّخَذُوا الشَّيَاطِينَ أَوْلِيَاءَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ وَيَحْسَبُونَ أَنَّهُم مُّهْتَدُونَ\nIndeed, they had taken the devils as allies instead of Allah while they thought that they were guided.\n[Al-A’raf: 30]\n2. The second ‘Aulia’ are the ones who have made Allah(swt) their ‘Wali’. The Holy Quran says about these:\n﴿أَلَا إِنَّ أَوْلِيَاءَ اللَّـهِ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ ٦٢﴾\nUnquestionably, [for] the allies of Allah there will be no fear concerning them, nor will they grieve.\n[Yunus: 62]\nAnd the excellence of these people has been mentioned as:\n﴿الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَكَانُوا يَتَّقُونَ ٦٣ لَهُمُ الْبُشْرَىٰ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ ۚ﴾\nThose who believed and were fearing Allah. For them are good tidings in the worldly life and in the Hereafter.\n[Yunus: 63, 64]\nThat is, on the Day of Judgement when the disbelievers and the polytheists will be running hither-thither terrified, the ‘Aulia’ of Allah(swt) will be calmly reading their book of deeds:\n﴿لَا يَحْزُنُهُمُ الْفَزَعُ الْأَكْبَرُ وَتَتَلَقَّاهُمُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ هَـٰذَا يَوْمُكُمُ الَّذِي كُنتُمْ تُوعَدُونَ ١٠٣﴾\nThey will not be grieved by the greatest terror, and the angels will meet them, [saying], \"This is your Day which you have been promised\"\n[Al-Anbiya: 103]\nThat is, the enemies of Islam will be running around in panic and will not find peace anywhere.\nIt is narrated by the companions regarding the ‘Aulia’ that when you see them, you remember Allah(swt); that is their behavior, character, interaction with others and their nature both within and without will be such that you are reminded of the Sovereignty of Allah(swt) and you exclaim, “Subhan Allah”.\nNow, when we have understood the ‘Aulia’ of Allah(swt), we need to take care to stay away from the ‘Aulia’ of satan who call us towards shirk, bida’at and superstitions. We should always try to analyse everything in the light of the Holy Quran and sahih hadith lest we lose the most precious wealth of this world and the Hereafter namely, Imaan.\nOne more virtue of the ‘Aulia’ of Allah(swt) is that they are not sad in this world; but cheerfully accept whatever is destined for them. They are not defeated by the sorrows of this world but take everything in their stride saying that whatever is happening is from Allah(swt) and are patient and forbearing. Their excellence is narrated in a sahih hadith:\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n\"There is a group of the slaves of Allah(swt) that even the Prophets and martyrs will envy,\" Then someone asked, \"Who are these people? Perhaps we can love them.\" And he(saws) said, \"They are a people who love each other through the light of Allah(swt) not through wealth or family ties. Their faces are filled with nur (light) and they are on pulpits of light, neither do they fear when the people fear nor do they grieve when the people grieve.\" Then the Prophet(saws) recited the verse:\n﴿أَلَا إِنَّ أَوْلِيَاءَ اللَّـهِ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ ٦٢﴾\nUnquestionably, [for] the allies of Allah there will be no fear concerning them, nor will they grieve.\n[Yunus: 62]\n(See: Sahih Ibn-Hibbaan, 573)\nThe gist is that the ‘Aulia’ of Allah(swt) are the people who follow the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith and make the lives of the companions and the Holy Prophet(saws) their model. ‘Aulia-e-Satan’ are the people who follow the ‘Zaeef’ and ‘Mauzoo’ hadith, blindly believe in mysticism even if it goes against the teachings of Islam and also follow various types of innovations in religion in order to gain honour among people. It is obligatory for a Muslim to keep away from such things."],[347,"§Wadd\nIn Surah-71, Nuh, Verse-23, five idols have been mentioned. Their names are: Wadd, Suwa’, Yaghuth, Ya’uq and Nasr. It is the view of the historians that these were some pious people from the tribe of Nuh(as). When they died someone suggested that their idols be made so that they could be remembered for ever. As time went on people started praying to these idols and then the satan misled them further and taught them various forms of worship. In this way, the pious people who worshipped Allah(swt) alone themselves started being worshipped. These idolators do not realize that other than Allah(swt) none can cause them any harm or benefit. In this context Nuh(as) said,\n﴿قَالَ نُوحٌ رَّبِّ إِنَّهُمْ عَصَوْنِي وَاتَّبَعُوا مَن لَّمْ يَزِدْهُ مَالُهُ وَوَلَدُهُ إِلَّا خَسَارًا ٢١ وَمَكَرُوا مَكْرًا كُبَّارًا ٢٢ وَقَالُوا لَا تَذَرُنَّ آلِهَتَكُمْ وَلَا تَذَرُنَّ وَدًّا وَلَا سُوَاعًا وَلَا يَغُوثَ وَيَعُوقَ وَنَسْرًا ٢٣﴾\nNoah said, \"My Lord, indeed they have disobeyed me and followed him whose wealth and children will not increase him except in loss. And they conspired an immense conspiracy. And said, 'Never leave your gods and never leave Wadd or Suwa' or Yaghuth and Ya'uq and Nasr.\n[Nuh: 21-23]\nImam Bukhari cites the narration of Ibn-Abbas that the idols of the tribe of Nuh(as) were later on worshipped by the Arabs. Wadd was worshipped by the tribe of Kalb of Daumat-al-Jandal, Suwa’ became the idol of the tribe of Bani Hudayl, Yaghuth the idol of the tribe of Murad, Ya’uq the idol of the tribe of Hamdan and Nasr the idol of the tribe of Himyar. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 4920)\nIt is possible that even in other countries this is how idol-worship started because ‘tawheed’ is inborn in men and it is due to the influence of the parents and the society that a man becomes a polytheist."],[348,"§War of Hunain\n‘Hunain’ is the name of a city located between Makkah and Taif. After the triumph of Muslims over Makkah, the chieftains of Hunain held a conference. They felt that Islam was spreading too fast and Makkah, from which the Holy Prophet(saws) and the believers had fled at one time had also become an Islamic city. So, it is possible that the Muslim army may try to capture Hunain. So, they decided to attack the Muslims. When the Holy Prophet(saws) got this information, he(saws) commanded his companions to go to Hunain. At that time the strength of the Muslim army was twelve thousand; ten thousand who had come from Madina and the remaining two thousand were the new entrants to Islam. This was the biggest Muslim army till that date. In 10 Shawwal, 8 A. H./ February 630 A. D., the Muslim army reached Hunain. But even before the battle had started the Muslims became very proud that they would definitely win that day. This did not please Allah(swt) because a Muslim never becomes proud, winning and losing is in the hands of Allah(swt). The Muslims should always have faith in Allah(swt) but strive to increase their strength. Allah(swt) commands in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَأَعِدُّوا لَهُم مَّا اسْتَطَعْتُم مِّن قُوَّةٍ وَمِن رِّبَاطِ الْخَيْلِ تُرْهِبُونَ بِهِ عَدُوَّ اللَّـهِ وَعَدُوَّكُمْ وَآخَرِينَ مِن دُونِهِمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَهُمُ اللَّـهُ يَعْلَمُهُمْ ۚ وَمَا تُنفِقُوا مِن شَيْءٍ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ يُوَفَّ إِلَيْكُمْ وَأَنتُمْ لَا تُظْلَمُونَ ٦٠﴾\nAnd prepare against them whatever you are able of power and of steeds of war by which you may terrify the enemy of Allah and your enemy and others besides them whom you do not know [but] whom Allah knows. And whatever you spend in the cause of Allah will be fully repaid to you, and you will not be wronged.\n[Al-Anfal: 60]\nAs soon as the battle started, the enemies who were hiding in the mountains and valleys started raining arrows on the Muslims and took the Muslim army totally unawares as they were expecting to fight in the open ground. This shook up the Muslim army and they started running away. But the Holy Prophet(saws) and a few of his companions bravely stayed at their places and at that time the Holy Prophet(saws) started saying:\n“I am a prophet who does not lie. I am the son of Abdul Muttalib.” And then the Holy Prophet(saws) told his paternal uncle Abbas(ra),” Go and call the Muslims.” On hearing the voice of Abbas(ra), one by one the Muslims started turning back and in just a few hours, the Muslim army was reassembled and waged a fierce attack on the enemies. The enemies were now surprised and the Muslim army finally defeated them. The following verses were revealed about this war:\n﴿لَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّـهُ فِي مَوَاطِنَ كَثِيرَةٍ ۙ وَيَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ ۙ إِذْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ كَثْرَتُكُمْ فَلَمْ تُغْنِ عَنكُمْ شَيْئًا وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْكُمُ الْأَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ ثُمَّ وَلَّيْتُم مُّدْبِرِينَ ٢٥ ثُمَّ أَنزَلَ اللَّـهُ سَكِينَتَهُ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِ وَعَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَأَنزَلَ جُنُودًا لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا وَعَذَّبَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ۚ وَذَٰلِكَ جَزَاءُ الْكَافِرِينَ ٢٦﴾\nAllah has already given you victory in many regions and [even] on the day of Hunayn, when your great number pleased you, but it did not avail you at all, and the earth was confining for you with its vastness; then you turned back, fleeing. Then Allah sent down His tranquillity upon His Messenger and upon the believers and sent down soldiers angels whom you did not see and punished those who disbelieved. And that is the recompense of the disbelievers.\n[At-Tawba: 25, 26]\nFour Muslims were martyred in this battle and seventy from the enemy army were killed. Six thousand were made captives who were freed later on and then all of them embraced Islam."],[349,"§War-booty\nIn the war fought for truth, the wealth which the Islamic army obtains from the enemies is called war-booty. Before Islam, this was forbidden for Jews and the Christians. The custom was to collect the spoils of the war in one place and then a fire would come from the skies and burn it. (See Bukhari 3124 and Muslim 1747)\nBut Islam has declared this as permissible and thus squashed all the out-dated laws of the ancient religions. While allowing the army to share the war-booty, Islam also emphasizes the need to include the poor and needy. The Holy Quran says:\nوَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّمَا غَنِمْتُم مِّن شَيْءٍ فَأَنَّ لِلَّهِ خُمُسَهُ وَلِلرَّسُولِ وَلِذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَالْيَتَامَىٰ وَالْمَسَاكِينِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ\nAnd know that anything you obtain of war booty - then indeed, for Allah is one fifth of it and for the Messenger and for [his] near relatives and the orphans, the needy, and the [stranded] traveler.\n[Al-Anfal: 41]\nThat is, the war-booty is to be divided into five parts, one part of which is for Allah(swt), His Messenger(saws) etc, while the remaining four parts are to be distributed among the army. But the wealth called ‘Faiy’, that is the wealth obtained by the Messenger(saws) from the enemies without any war taking place is only for Allah(swt), His Messenger(saws) and his relatives, orphans, the poor and the traveller so that the wealth does not circulate only among the rich. (See: Quran, Surah-59, Al-Hashr, Verse-7)\nThat is, the army has no share in this wealth. When it is said that the wealth is for Allah(swt) and His Messenger(saws), it means the ‘Baitul-Maal’ or the royal treasury out of which the poor and the needy are helped. In this way the wonderful religion of Islam makes sure that the wealth does not remain only with the rich but also helps the poor and the needy. If somebody does not have the means of livelihood, then they can be helped out from the ‘Baitul-Maal’."],[350,"§Will\n‘Will’ is the bequest which a person makes and which comes into effect after the death of the person making the will. In the beginning it was compulsory as it says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذَا حَضَرَ أَحَدَكُمُ الْمَوْتُ إِن تَرَكَ خَيْرًا الْوَصِيَّةُ لِلْوَالِدَيْنِ وَالْأَقْرَبِينَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ ۖ حَقًّا عَلَى الْمُتَّقِينَ ١٨٠﴾\nPrescribed for you when death approaches [any] one of you if he leaves wealth [is that he should make] a bequest for the parents and near relatives according to what is acceptable - a duty upon the righteous.\n[Al-Baqara: 180]\nBut when the rules of inheritance were made, it was no longer compulsory. And the second thing is that inheritance cannot be made to the heirs as is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Allah(swt) has decided the share of the heirs and therefore bequests cannot be made to the heirs.” (Abu Dawood, 2853, Tirmizi,2203, Ibn-Majah, 2713)\nImportance of a will:\nNow it is forbidden to make a will; but he may make bequests to the relatives or may give something for some good work. In fact this is very important as is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n\"It is not permissible for any Muslim who has something to will to stay for two nights without having his last will and testament written and kept ready with him.\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 2738 and Sahih Muslim, 1627)\nBecause of the importance of a will, a grandson has not been made an heir to the paternal grandfather. The grandfather may give as much as he wishes to the grandson during his lifetime and can then bequeath something in his will. If the grandson had been an heir, then the grandfather would not have been able to bequeath anything to him.\nThe shares in the inheritance:\nThe purpose of making a will should not be to cheat the legal heirs of their share of the inheritance as is explained in Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-12. That is why it is allowed to will only one-third of the wealth. The remaining two-thirds will be distributed among the legal heirs as is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Will can be made only for one-third of the wealth and that is substantial.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1295 and Sahih Muslim, 1628)\nIt is narrated in the same hadith that it is better to leave one’s heirs rich rather than have them begging.\nThat is why, if one does not have much wealth, then it is better not to make a will but leave it to the legal heirs as many of the companions of the Holy Prophet(saws) did not leave a will."],[351,"§Wolf\nWolf is a wild animal which tears and eats its prey. That is why the people who loot and cruel and unjust people are compared to wolves. For example in the Bible, when Yaqub(as) was on his deathbed, he summoned his sons to him and told each one of them what the future had in store for them. He says about Benjamin, the younger brother of Yusuf(as)\n“Benjamin is a ravenous wolf; in the morning he devours the prey, in the evening he divides the plunder.”\n(See: Bible, Genesis, 49:27)\nYaqub(as) means the sons of Benjamin here because we come to know from the Bible that in the war between the Bani-Israel and the Benjamites, the sons of Benjamin came out of Gibeah and on the same day killed twenty-two thousand Israelites. (See: Bible, Judges, 20:21)\nIn the Surah-12 of the Holy Quran, the word ‘wolf’ has been used three times in the story of Yusuf(as). It has first been used when the brothers of Yusuf(as) ask their father to send Yusuf(as) with them:\nFirst time:\n﴿أَرْسِلْهُ مَعَنَا غَدًا يَرْتَعْ وَيَلْعَبْ وَإِنَّا لَهُ لَحَافِظُونَ ١٢ قَالَ إِنِّي لَيَحْزُنُنِي أَن تَذْهَبُوا بِهِ وَأَخَافُ أَن يَأْكُلَهُ الذِّئْبُ وَأَنتُمْ عَنْهُ غَافِلُونَ ١٣﴾\nSend him with us tomorrow that he may eat well and play. And indeed, we will be his guardians. [Jacob] said, \"Indeed, it saddens me that you should take him, and I fear that a wolf would eat him while you are of him unaware.\"\nSecond time:\n﴿قَالُوا لَئِنْ أَكَلَهُ الذِّئْبُ وَنَحْنُ عُصْبَةٌ إِنَّا إِذًا لَّخَاسِرُونَ ١٤ فَلَمَّا ذَهَبُوا بِهِ وَأَجْمَعُوا أَن يَجْعَلُوهُ فِي غَيَابَتِ الْجُبِّ ۚ وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْهِ لَتُنَبِّئَنَّهُم بِأَمْرِهِمْ هَٰذَا وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ١٥﴾\nThey said, \"If a wolf should eat him while we are a [strong] clan, indeed, we would then be losers.\" So when they took him [out] and agreed to put him into the bottom of the well... But We inspired to him, \"You will surely inform them [someday] about this affair of theirs while they do not perceive [your identity].\"\nThird time:\n﴿وَجَاءُوا أَبَاهُمْ عِشَاءً يَبْكُونَ ١٦ قَالُوا يَا أَبَانَا إِنَّا ذَهَبْنَا نَسْتَبِقُ وَتَرَكْنَا يُوسُفَ عِندَ مَتَاعِنَا فَأَكَلَهُ الذِّئْبُ ۖ وَمَا أَنتَ بِمُؤْمِنٍ لَّنَا وَلَوْ كُنَّا صَادِقِينَ ١٧﴾\nAnd they came to their father at night, weeping. They said, \"O our father, indeed we went racing each other and left Joseph with our possessions, and a wolf ate him. But you would not believe us, even if we were truthful.\"\n[Yusuf: 12-17]\n(For more information see ‘Yusuf(as)’)"],[352,"§Wood-Worm\nWe had earlier translated ‘Daabba’ as a creature who walks the earth. But in surah Saba of the Holy Quran, it is used to mean a worm of the earth (termite):\n﴿فَلَمَّا قَضَيْنَا عَلَيْهِ الْمَوْتَ مَا دَلَّهُمْ عَلَىٰ مَوْتِهِ إِلَّا دَابَّةُ الْأَرْضِ تَأْكُلُ مِنسَأَتَهُ ۖ فَلَمَّا خَرَّ تَبَيَّنَتِ الْجِنُّ أَن لَّوْ كَانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ الْغَيْبَ مَا لَبِثُوا فِي الْعَذَابِ الْمُهِينِ ١٤﴾\nThen, when We decreed (Solomon's) death, nothing showed them his death except a little worm of the earth, which kept (slowly) gnawing away at his staff: so when he fell down, the Jinns saw plainly that if they had known the unseen, they would not have tarried in the humiliating Penalty (of their Task).\n[Saba: 14]\n(For more information see ‘Sulaiman(as)’)."],[353,"§Yaghuth\n‘Yaghuth’ was the name of an idol who was worshipped by An’um, a branch of the Tay tribe and many branches of the Madhhij tribe. The people of Madhhij had established this idol at Jursh, between Yemen and Hijaz. This idol resembled a lion. (For more information see: ‘Wadd’)"],[354,"§Yahya(as)\nYahya(as) was a great prophet and had great self-restraint. (See: Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-40)\nYahya(as) and Isa(as) were born in the same year. Yahya(as) was six months elder to Isa(as). Zachariah who was from the descendants of Ibraheem(as), was the father of Yahya(as). His mother was Elizabeth or Elisheva who was a descendant of Haroon(as) and therefore from the family of Ibraheem(as). But Elizabeth was barren. (See: Injeel, Luke 1:5-7)\nElizabeth was the maternal aunt of Maryam. According to another view she was her sister.\nThe birth of Yahya(as) was a miracle because his mother was barren and his father had become old. Then it so happened that Zachariah was made the guardian of Maryam because Maryam’s mother had made a vow that her daughter would serve in the mosque of Masjid-e-Aqsa and worship Allah(swt). The Holy Quran says:\n﴿فَتَقَبَّلَهَا رَبُّهَا بِقَبُولٍ حَسَنٍ وَأَنبَتَهَا نَبَاتًا حَسَنًا وَكَفَّلَهَا زَكَرِيَّا ۖ كُلَّمَا دَخَلَ عَلَيْهَا زَكَرِيَّا الْمِحْرَابَ وَجَدَ عِندَهَا رِزْقًا ۖ قَالَ يَا مَرْيَمُ أَنَّىٰ لَكِ هَـٰذَا ۖ قَالَتْ هُوَ مِنْ عِندِ اللَّـهِ ۖ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَرْزُقُ مَن يَشَاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ ٣٧ هُنَالِكَ دَعَا زَكَرِيَّا رَبَّهُ ۖ قَالَ رَبِّ هَبْ لِي مِن لَّدُنكَ ذُرِّيَّةً طَيِّبَةً ۖ إِنَّكَ سَمِيعُ الدُّعَاءِ ٣٨﴾\nSo her Lord accepted her with good acceptance and caused her to grow in a good manner and put her in the care of Zechariah. Every time Zechariah entered upon her in the prayer chamber, he found with her provision. He said, \"O Mary, from where is this [coming] to you?\" She said, \"It is from Allah. Indeed, Allah provides for whom He wills without account.\" At that, Zechariah called upon his Lord, saying, \"My Lord, grant me from Yourself a good offspring. Indeed, You are the Hearer of supplication.\"\n[Al-i-Imran: 37, 38]\nIt was the desire of Zachariah to have a son who would preach to his tribe after Zachariah’s death because he saw the Bani-Israel indulging in all sorts of evil. They had abandoned monotheism which was the main principle preached by their ancestors and all the prophets and had become idol-worshippers. But seeing that his wife was barren and he had grown old, he had kept his wish suppressed. But when he saw that Maryam was being provided by Allah(swt) with good things, some of which were not even in season, he mustered the courage to pray to Allah(swt) for a son. At another place in the Holy Quran, the story of Zachariah is described as under:\n﴿ذِكْرُ رَحْمَتِ رَبِّكَ عَبْدَهُ زَكَرِيَّا ٢ إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُ نِدَاءً خَفِيًّا ٣ قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي وَهَنَ الْعَظْمُ مِنِّي وَاشْتَعَلَ الرَّأْسُ شَيْبًا وَلَمْ أَكُن بِدُعَائِكَ رَبِّ شَقِيًّا ٤ وَإِنِّي خِفْتُ الْمَوَالِيَ مِن وَرَائِي وَكَانَتِ امْرَأَتِي عَاقِرًا فَهَبْ لِي مِن لَّدُنكَ وَلِيًّا ٥ يَرِثُنِي وَيَرِثُ مِنْ آلِ يَعْقُوبَ ۖ وَاجْعَلْهُ رَبِّ رَضِيًّا ٦ يَا زَكَرِيَّا إِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلَامٍ اسْمُهُ يَحْيَىٰ لَمْ نَجْعَل لَّهُ مِن قَبْلُ سَمِيًّا ٧ قَالَ رَبِّ أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لِي غُلَامٌ وَكَانَتِ امْرَأَتِي عَاقِرًا وَقَدْ بَلَغْتُ مِنَ الْكِبَرِ عِتِيًّا ٨ قَالَ كَذَٰلِكَ قَالَ رَبُّكَ هُوَ عَلَيَّ هَيِّنٌ وَقَدْ خَلَقْتُكَ مِن قَبْلُ وَلَمْ تَكُ شَيْئًا ٩ قَالَ رَبِّ اجْعَل لِّي آيَةً ۚ قَالَ آيَتُكَ أَلَّا تُكَلِّمَ النَّاسَ ثَلَاثَ لَيَالٍ سَوِيًّا ١٠ فَخَرَجَ عَلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ مِنَ الْمِحْرَابِ فَأَوْحَىٰ إِلَيْهِمْ أَن سَبِّحُوا بُكْرَةً وَعَشِيًّا ١١ يَا يَحْيَىٰ خُذِ الْكِتَابَ بِقُوَّةٍ ۖ وَآتَيْنَاهُ الْحُكْمَ صَبِيًّا ١٢ وَحَنَانًا مِّن لَّدُنَّا وَزَكَاةً ۖ وَكَانَ تَقِيًّا ١٣ وَبَرًّا بِوَالِدَيْهِ وَلَمْ يَكُن جَبَّارًا عَصِيًّا ١٤ وَسَلَامٌ عَلَيْهِ يَوْمَ وُلِدَ وَيَوْمَ يَمُوتُ وَيَوْمَ يُبْعَثُ حَيًّا ١٥﴾\n[This is] a mention of the mercy of your Lord to His servant Zechariah. When he called to his Lord a private supplication. He said, \"My Lord, indeed my bones have weakened, and my head has filled with white, and never have I been in my supplication to You, my Lord, unhappy. And indeed, I fear the successors after me, and my wife has been barren, so give me from Yourself an heir. Who will inherit me and inherit from the family of Jacob. And make him, my Lord, pleasing [to You].\" [He was told], \"O Zechariah, indeed We give you good tidings of a boy whose name will be John. We have not assigned to any before [this] name.\" He said, \"My Lord, how will I have a boy when my wife has been barren and I have reached extreme old age?\" [An angel] said, \"Thus [it will be]; your Lord says, 'It is easy for Me, for I created you before, while you were nothing.' \" [Zechariah] said, \"My Lord, make for me a sign.\" He said, \"Your sign is that you will not speak to the people for three nights, [being] sound.\" So he came out to his people from the prayer chamber and signaled to them to exalt [Allah] in the morning and afternoon. [Allah] said, \"O John, take the Scripture with determination.\" And We gave him judgement [while yet] a boy. And affection from Us and purity, and he was fearing of Allah. And dutiful to his parents, and he was not a disobedient tyrant. And peace be upon him the day he was born and the day he dies and the day he is raised alive.\n[Maryam: 2-15]\nWhen Yahya(as) grew up, he wore a cloth made of camel-hair and went away into the forests. There he spent time in the worship of Allah(swt) and sometimes came to the city to preach the message of Allah(swt). He asked them to repent for their sins (see: Injeel Luke 3:4-5) and warned them of the punishment of Allah(swt). In the Holy Quran the word ‘Hasur’ is used which means that he had no desire for women. (See: Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-39)\nYahya(as) was only thirty when Herod the tyrant king of Palestine had him killed which is described in the book Matthew of Injeel. (See: Injeel Matthew 14:1-11)\nYahya(as) was among the prophets who met the Holy Prophet(saws) on the second heaven on the night of ‘Meraj’. (See: Sahih Bukhari 3207 and Sahih Muslim, 164)"],[355,"§Yajooj and Majooj (Gog and Magog)\nThis was a riotous and unruly tribe. It has been described at two places in the Holy Quran. In Surah-18, Al-Kahf, it has been described as:\n﴿قَالُوا يَا ذَا الْقَرْنَيْنِ إِنَّ يَأْجُوجَ وَمَأْجُوجَ مُفْسِدُونَ فِي الْأَرْضِ فَهَلْ نَجْعَلُ لَكَ خَرْجًا عَلَىٰ أَن تَجْعَلَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَهُمْ سَدًّا ٩٤ قَالَ مَا مَكَّنِّي فِيهِ رَبِّي خَيْرٌ فَأَعِينُونِي بِقُوَّةٍ أَجْعَلْ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ رَدْمًا ٩٥ آتُونِي زُبَرَ الْحَدِيدِ ۖ حَتَّىٰ إِذَا سَاوَىٰ بَيْنَ الصَّدَفَيْنِ قَالَ انفُخُوا ۖ حَتَّىٰ إِذَا جَعَلَهُ نَارًا قَالَ آتُونِي أُفْرِغْ عَلَيْهِ قِطْرًا ٩٦ فَمَا اسْطَاعُوا أَن يَظْهَرُوهُ وَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوا لَهُ نَقْبًا ٩٧ قَالَ هَـٰذَا رَحْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّي ۖ فَإِذَا جَاءَ وَعْدُ رَبِّي جَعَلَهُ دَكَّاءَ ۖ وَكَانَ وَعْدُ رَبِّي حَقًّا ٩٨﴾\nThey said, \"O Dhul-Qarnayn, indeed Gog and Magog are [great] corrupters in the land. So may we assign for you an expenditure that you might make between us and them a barrier?\" He said, \"That in which my Lord has established me is better [than what you offer], but assist me with strength; I will make between you and them a dam. Bring me sheets of iron\" - until, when he had leveled [them] between the two mountain walls, he said, \"Blow [with bellows],\" until when he had made it [like] fire, he said, \"Bring me, that I may pour over it molten copper.\" So Gog and Magog were unable to pass over it, nor were they able [to effect] in it any penetration. [Dhul-Qarnayn] said, \"This is a mercy from my Lord; but when the promise of my Lord comes, He will make it level, and ever is the promise of my Lord true.\"\n[Al-Kahf: 94-98]\nIn the second place it has been described as:\n﴿حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فُتِحَتْ يَأْجُوجُ وَمَأْجُوجُ وَهُم مِّن كُلِّ حَدَبٍ يَنسِلُونَ ٩٦﴾\nUntil when [the dam of] Gog and Magog has been opened and they, from every elevation, descend.\n[Al-Anbiya: 96]\nWho are these Yajooj and Majooj (Gog and Magog)? The scholars have various views in this regard. As they have been described in the Bible also, let us first see what it says about them:\nThe sons of Japheth: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshek and Tiras.\n(Bible, Genesis, 10:2 and 1 Chronicles 1:5)\nI will send fire on Magog and on those who live in safety in the coastlands, and they will know that I am the Lord.\n(Bible, Ezekiel 39:6)\n“Son of man, set your face against Gog, of the land of Magog”\n(See: Ezekiel, 38:2)\nEven from the Bible we do not get information about this tribe or the place of its habitation. When we study history in the light of the information from the Holy Quran, we understand that it was an unruly and uncivilized tribe who caused havoc among the mountain-dwelling tribes. That is why the people who were tormented approached Zul-qarnain and asked him to build a dam for them. Among the known dams is the one found to the east of the Caspian sea in Qafqaz. The second one is in Asia about one hundred and fifty miles to the south of Buqara which has been described by the European explorer Marco Polo, the details of which can be found in Encyclopedia of Britannica, part 13, p. 526. According to Moulana Abul Kalam Azad, this was a Mongolian tribe which was called ‘Gog’ in Chinese. This ‘gog’ became popular as ‘Mog’ among the Greek in 600 B. C. and started being called ‘Magog’. And it became ‘Majooj’ in the Hebrew language. Even today they are called Gog and Magog in Europe.\nIn the same way there was a clan named ‘Yuch-chi’ in ancient China. It is possible that this slowly became ‘Yajooj’. Briefly we can say that this was some uncivilized tribe of northern Asia who attacked and plundered the civilized kingdoms. When Zul-qarnain reached this place in his expeditions, seeing that he was a very just and merciful king, people asked him to build a wall to protect them against these tribes. He acceded to their request and thus the people started living peacefully.\nOne of the signs of Doomsday is that this wall will break down and the Yajooj-Majooj will again spread havoc everywhere. Then Allah(swt) will destroy the Yajooj-Majooj with the help of a creature in their necks and they will be killed just as Jaraad was killed. But the believers will be safe from the torments of these Yajooj-Majooj as it is narrated in Sahih Bukhari that even after they arrive, the believers will be performing the Hajj and Umra of Baitullah. (See: Sahih Bukhari:1598)\nFrom the description of Yajooj-Majooj in the Holy Quran, we can infer the following:\n1. Zul-qarnain about whom the Jews question the Holy Prophet(saws) in order to test him (and whom the Jews were very well acquainted with) so truthfully and easily says that whatever has been done is due to Allah(swt) alone and His mercy. (See: Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-98)\nHe was not proud or arrogant like the disbelievers of Makka.\nAnd secondly, he never said that the wall or dam built by him will never break but in fact said that when the command of Allah(swt) comes, it will be destroyed just like this entire world will be scattered. There is a lesson in this for those who are proud of what they do and think that they are indestructible. The power of Allah(swt) is beyond our comprehension and when He(swt) can destroy the earth and the skies then a mere wall is just nothing.\nIn fact we come to know from sahih hadith that already a hole has been made in it. (See: Sahih Bukhari:3346 and Sahih Muslim 2880)\nThe fact that a hole has been made in it is one of the minor signs of Doomsday. Before Doomsday the wall will be blown to smithereens and the Yajooj-Majooj will emerge and create mayhem.\nAll these are the ‘unseen’ or ‘ghaib’ things which we as believers have to believe. Our limited knowledge and comprehension cannot encompass the unlimited things."],[356,"§Ya’uq\n‘Ya’uq’ was the idol of the tribe of Hamdan. (For more information see: ‘Wadd’)"],[357,"§Yaqub(as)\nYaqub(as) was the grandson of Ibraheem(as) and the son of Ishaq(as). Yaqub(as) was born in 1836 B. C. in the city of Habrun, now called Khaleel. He had a twin brother Isu. As the brothers did not get along, Yaqub(as) left Habrun and went away to his maternal uncle in Fidaan Aram near the city of Harraan. There he got married. Yaqub(as) had four wives: Leah, Rachel, Bilhah and Zilpah. He had twelve sons from them:\nReuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Dan, Naphtali, Issachar, Zebulun, Asher, Yusuf, Benjamin, Gad and a daughter Dina. Then, he went to Baitul-Muqaddas. He lived there for some time and when there was a drought in Palestine, he went away to Egypt with his family. He was 130 years old at that time. He lived in Egypt for seventeen years and then passed away. He was 147 years old when he died. Hunoot (rubbing camphor) was done to the body of Yaqub(as) and then his sons brought it to Habrun and buried it there. Before his death, Yaqub(as) prayed for Yusuf and his offspring and then for all his offspring.\nAllah(swt) made Yaqub(as) a prophet and sent him to his people. It is described as follows in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِنَّا أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْكَ كَمَا أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ نُوحٍ وَالنَّبِيِّينَ مِن بَعْدِهِ ۚ وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَإِسْمَاعِيلَ وَإِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَالْأَسْبَاطِ وَعِيسَىٰ وَأَيُّوبَ وَيُونُسَ وَهَارُونَ وَسُلَيْمَانَ ۚ وَآتَيْنَا دَاوُودَ زَبُورًا ١٦٣﴾\nIndeed, We have revealed to you, [O Muhammad], as We revealed to Noah and the prophets after him. And we revealed to Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, the Descendants, Jesus, Job, Jonah, Aaron, and Solomon, and to David We gave the book [of Psalms].\n[An-Nisa: 163]\nLike all the other true prophets, Yaqub(as) invited people towards the worship of the One true Allah(swt) and forbade the worshipping of other things. Yaqub(as) himself was always engrossed in the worship of Allah(swt) and stopped people from worshipping various gods and goddesses. He spoke to his sons on his deathbed:\n﴿أَمْ كُنتُمْ شُهَدَاءَ إِذْ حَضَرَ يَعْقُوبَ الْمَوْتُ إِذْ قَالَ لِبَنِيهِ مَا تَعْبُدُونَ مِن بَعْدِي قَالُوا نَعْبُدُ إِلَـٰهَكَ وَإِلَـٰهَ آبَائِكَ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَإِسْمَاعِيلَ وَإِسْحَاقَ إِلَـٰهًا وَاحِدًا وَنَحْنُ لَهُ مُسْلِمُونَ ١٣٣﴾\nOr were you witnesses when death approached Jacob, when he said to his sons, \"What will you worship after me?\" They said, \"We will worship your God and the God of your fathers, Abraham and Ishmael and Isaac - one God. And we are Muslims [in submission] to Him.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 133]\nAllah(swt) was very merciful to the family of Yaqub(as):\n﴿وَكَذَٰلِكَ يَجْتَبِيكَ رَبُّكَ وَيُعَلِّمُكَ مِن تَأْوِيلِ الْأَحَادِيثِ وَيُتِمُّ نِعْمَتَهُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلَىٰ آلِ يَعْقُوبَ كَمَا أَتَمَّهَا عَلَىٰ أَبَوَيْكَ مِن قَبْلُ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَإِسْحَاقَ ۚ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ ٦﴾\nAnd thus will your Lord choose you and teach you the interpretation of narratives and complete His favor upon you and upon the family of Jacob, as He completed it upon your fathers before, Abraham and Isaac. Indeed, your Lord is Knowing and Wise.\"\n[Yusuf: 6]\nAnd Allah(swt) completed the favour by continuing the chain of prophethood in the family of Ishaq(as) and Yaqub(as). The Holy Quran says:\nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهُ إِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَجَعَلْنَا فِي ذُرِّيَّتِهِ النُّبُوَّةَ وَالْكِتَابَ\nAnd We gave to Him Isaac and Jacob and placed in his descendants prophethood and scripture.\n[Al-Ankabut: 27]\nYusuf(as) was also from this family. That is Yusuf(as), the son of Yaqub(as), the son of Ishaq(as), the son of Ibraheem(as). Perhaps, there is no other instance in the world where four prophets were from the same family one after the other.\nYaqub(as) is also called Israel and that is why his descendants are called the Bani-Israel. He has been described in great detail in the Holy Quran. We come to know from the Taurah that it was Allah(swt)’s command to name him Israel."],[358,"§Ya-Sin\nSee ‘Alif-Laam-Meem’."],[359,"§Yehezkiel\nHe was a famous prophet of Bani-Israel. He was a contemporary of prophet Jeremiah who lived in the 6th century B. C. He is not mentioned by name in the Holy Quran, but one story seems to be of Yehezkiel(as):\n﴿أَوْ كَالَّذِي مَرَّ عَلَىٰ قَرْيَةٍ وَهِيَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلَىٰ عُرُوشِهَا قَالَ أَنَّىٰ يُحْيِي هَـٰذِهِ اللَّـهُ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا ۖ فَأَمَاتَهُ اللَّـهُ مِائَةَ عَامٍ ثُمَّ بَعَثَهُ ۖ قَالَ كَمْ لَبِثْتَ ۖ قَالَ لَبِثْتُ يَوْمًا أَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ ۖ قَالَ بَل لَّبِثْتَ مِائَةَ عَامٍ فَانظُرْ إِلَىٰ طَعَامِكَ وَشَرَابِكَ لَمْ يَتَسَنَّهْ ۖ وَانظُرْ إِلَىٰ حِمَارِكَ وَلِنَجْعَلَكَ آيَةً لِّلنَّاسِ ۖ وَانظُرْ إِلَى الْعِظَامِ كَيْفَ نُنشِزُهَا ثُمَّ نَكْسُوهَا لَحْمًا ۚ فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ قَالَ أَعْلَمُ أَنَّ اللَّـهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ ٢٥٩﴾\nOr [consider such an example] as the one who passed by a township which had fallen into ruin. He said, \"How will Allah bring this to life after its death?\" So Allah caused him to die for a hundred years; then He revived him. He said, \"How long have you remained?\" The man said, \"I have remained a day or part of a day.\" He said, \"Rather, you have remained one hundred years. Look at your food and your drink; it has not changed with time. And look at your donkey; and We will make you a sign for the people. And look at the bones [of this donkey] - how We raise them and then We cover them with flesh.\" And when it became clear to him, he said, \"I know that Allah is over all things competent.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 259]\nHis detailed life-history cannot be found even in the Bible. But there is a story about some dry bones which goes as follows:\nThe hand of the Lord was on me, and he brought me out by the Spirit of the Lord and set me in the middle of a valley; it was full of bones. 2 He led me back and forth among them, and I saw a great many bones on the floor of the valley, bones that were very dry. 3 He asked me, “Son of man, can these bones live?”\nI said, “Sovereign Lord, you alone know.”\n4 Then he said to me, “Prophesy to these bones and say to them, ‘Dry bones, hear the word of the Lord! 5 This is what the Sovereign Lord says to these bones: I will make breath[a] enter you, and you will come to life. 6 I will attach tendons to you and make flesh come upon you and cover you with skin; I will put breath in you, and you will come to life. Then you will know that I am the Lord.’”\n(Bible, Ezekiel 37:1-6)\nThe above two descriptions from the Holy Quran and the Bible have a lot of similarities albeit these bones were of the Bani-Israel.\nAs for the city which had been totally destroyed, we understand from the Bible that Baitul-Muqaddas was totally ruined for a hundred years by the Persian king and then Bukht Nasar and not even one house was left standing. On seeing the city it was difficult to imagine that it could be rebuilt. The things left incomplete in the Bible were completed in the Holy Quran because the Holy Quran is the final, last and complete divine book which confirms all the previous books. It corrects the distortions in the previous books. The Holy Quran says:\nوَأَنزَلْنَا إِلَيْكَ الْكِتَابَ بِالْحَقِّ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مِنَ الْكِتَابِ وَمُهَيْمِنًا عَلَيْهِ\nAnd We have revealed to you, [O Muhammad], the Book in truth, confirming that which preceded it of the Scripture and as a criterion over it.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 48]\nAs many distortions have been made in all the previous divine books, the Holy Quran remains the only firm rope which we should hold on to and it shall remain so till Doomsday and in the Hereafter. That is why the word ‘Muhaymin’ has been used for the Holy Quran as it is the only means of distinguishing the original teachings of the divine books."],[360,"§Yunus(as)\nYunus(as) was a great prophet of the Bani-Israel. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَإِنَّ يُونُسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ١٣٩﴾\nAnd indeed, Jonah was among the messengers.\n[As-Saffat: 139]\nHe was born in Syria. But he was commanded by Allah(swt) to go to a tribe who numbered more than one lakh. [As-Saffat: 147]. The Holy Quran does not mention the tribe or the place where they lived but from the Bible we understand that it was the city of Nineveh, situated on the banks of river Tigris in Iraq and was the capital of the Assyrian empire. There is a book about Yunus(as) in the Bible. (See: Jonah, 1:2, 3:2-5)\nThis is confirmed by one hadith also. When the Holy Prophet(saws) went to Taif and the people there stoned him, he(saws) entered the garden of Utba and Shaiba-bin-Rabi’a to take rest. Blood was coming out of his feet. Utba and Shaiba asked their servant Addas to take something to the wounded man to eat and drink. Before eating the Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Bismillah”. Addas was surprised and asked the Holy Prophet(saws), “The people over here do not say Bismillah before eating.” The Holy Prophet(saws) asked him, “From which place are you and what is your religion?”\nAddas replied, “I am a Christian and I am from Nineveh.” The Holy Prophet(saws) then said, “So you are from the place of my brother Yunus-bin-Amittai.” Addas asked him, “Do you know who Yunus-bin-Amittai is?” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “He is my brother who was a prophet and even I am a prophet.” On hearing this, Addas fell at the feet of the Holy Prophet(saws) and started kissing his head and hands and feet and became a Muslim. (See: Moaz-Mussahaba by Abu Nuzaim 2377 and Seerat Ibn Hisham 1:419-422). But the sanad is ‘Mursal’.\nNow the question arises as to why a prophet of the Bani-Israel was sent to Nineveh? If we accept what the Bible says as true, then the answer is that maybe some of the people of Bani-Israel lived there. And true to their nature they had started worshipping the gods and goddesses of the Ashurites because we come to know from the history of the Bani-Israel that they very easily give up monotheism in favour of idolatry. It is the Infinite mercy of Allah(swt) that He(swt) warned them again and again by sending prophets from time to time.\nThere was a great Assyrian empire about five hundred miles from Palestine where the people were worshipping idols instead of Allah(swt) and indulged in all sorts of sins. So, even though Yunus(as) was from Bani-Israel, Allah(swt) sent him to these people for their guidance. The Holy Quran says:\nإِنَّمَا أَنتَ مُنذِرٌ ۖ وَلِكُلِّ قَوْمٍ هَادٍ\nYou are only a warner, and for every people is a guide.\n[Ar-Ra’ad: 7]\n﴿إِنْ أَنتَ إِلَّا نَذِيرٌ ٢٣ إِنَّا أَرْسَلْنَاكَ بِالْحَقِّ بَشِيرًا وَنَذِيرًا ۚ وَإِن مِّنْ أُمَّةٍ إِلَّا خَلَا فِيهَا نَذِيرٌ ٢٤﴾\nYou, [O Muhammad], are not but a warner. Indeed, We have sent you with the truth as a bringer of good tidings and a warner. And there was no nation but that there had passed within it a warner.\n[Fatir: 23-24]\nThat is why the Assyrians are known as the tribe of Yunus(as) and their ruins are found even today towards the east of river Tigris.\nThere seems to be a flaw in the Bible which says that Yunus(as) did not go to Nineveh but disobeyed Allah(swt) and went away towards Tarsheesh and a fish swallowed him when there was a cyclone.\nIt does not befit a prophet to go against the command of Allah(swt). So, the truth is that Yunus(as) did go to Nineveh and conveyed the message of Allah(swt) to those people. He forbade idol-worship but those people were adamant. They rejected the message of Yunus(as) and troubled him in various ways. This happened around 790 B. C.\nThen, giving up his mission, Yunus(as) prayed to Allah(swt) to punish them and went away from Nineveh thinking that the punishment was near. After Yunus(as) left, the people of Nineveh feared that the punishment would come and repented to Allah(swt) and embraced Islam. In this way they were saved from the punishment of Allah(swt). Allah(swt) commands in the Holy Quran:\n﴿فَلَوْلَا كَانَتْ قَرْيَةٌ آمَنَتْ فَنَفَعَهَا إِيمَانُهَا إِلَّا قَوْمَ يُونُسَ لَمَّا آمَنُوا كَشَفْنَا عَنْهُمْ عَذَابَ الْخِزْيِ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا وَمَتَّعْنَاهُمْ إِلَىٰ حِينٍ ٩٨﴾\nThen has there not been a [single] city that believed so its faith benefited it except the people of Jonah? When they believed, We removed from them the punishment of disgrace in worldly life and gave them enjoyment for a time.\n[Yunus: 98]\nIt is the rule of Allah(swt) that one cannot turn a believer on seeing the punishment because the time for the test would’ve passed and so it is the same whether the person believes or not. But this rule did not apply to the tribe of Yunus(as) because Yunus(as) cursed and left them before the command from Allah(swt) came. So, Allah(swt) saved them from punishment and as a warning He(swt) made a fish swallow up Yunus(as):\n﴿إِذْ أَبَقَ إِلَى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُونِ ١٤٠ فَسَاهَمَ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُدْحَضِينَ ١٤١ فَالْتَقَمَهُ الْحُوتُ وَهُوَ مُلِيمٌ ١٤٢ فَلَوْلَا أَنَّهُ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُسَبِّحِينَ ١٤٣ لَلَبِثَ فِي بَطْنِهِ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ ١٤٤ فَنَبَذْنَاهُ بِالْعَرَاءِ وَهُوَ سَقِيمٌ ١٤٥ وَأَنبَتْنَا عَلَيْهِ شَجَرَةً مِّن يَقْطِينٍ ١٤٦﴾\n[Mention] when he ran away to the laden ship. And he drew lots and was among the losers. Then the fish swallowed him, while he was blameworthy. And had he not been of those who exalt Allah, He would have remained inside its belly until the Day they are resurrected. But We threw him onto the open shore while he was ill. And We caused to grow over him a gourd vine. [As-Saffat: 140-146]\nThe gourd vine was for shading Yunus(as) and maybe it bore fruit also which he could eat and get well. Now the question is, which was the fish which could swallow a human being whole? And which was the sea in which this incident occurred? The fish was the whale which is more than twenty feet long. It does not eat humans but can swallow them. A few years back there was an incident where a whale swallowed a fisherman and he was alive in its stomach for seven hours. As for the sea in which this event of Yunus(as) occurred, he went to Palestine, furious with the people of Nineveh. Then, he got onto a ship going from the port Yafa to the port of Tarsheesh when there was a storm in the Mediterranean sea and this event occurred. This is confirmed even in the Bible. (See: Bible, Jonah,1:3)\nWhy did Yunus(as) have to undergo this trial? It says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَذَا النُّونِ إِذ ذَّهَبَ مُغَاضِبًا فَظَنَّ أَن لَّن نَّقْدِرَ عَلَيْهِ فَنَادَىٰ فِي الظُّلُمَاتِ أَن لَّا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا أَنتَ سُبْحَانَكَ إِنِّي كُنتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ ٨٧ فَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهُ وَنَجَّيْنَاهُ مِنَ الْغَمِّ ۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نُنجِي الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ٨٨﴾\nAnd [mention] the man of the fish, when he went off in anger and thought that We would not decree [anything] upon him. And he called out within the darknesses, \"There is no deity except You; exalted are You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers.\" So We responded to him and saved him from the distress. And thus do We save the believers.\n[Al-Anbiya: 87, 88]\nNarrating the story of Yunus(as), Allah(swt) is consoling the Holy Prophet(saws) to have patience in the face of the torments of the disbelievers of Makka and not be impatient in the matter:\n﴿فَاصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تَكُن كَصَاحِبِ الْحُوتِ إِذْ نَادَىٰ وَهُوَ مَكْظُومٌ ٤٨﴾\nThen be patient for the decision of your Lord, [O Muhammad], and be not like the companion of the fish when he called out while he was distressed.\n[Al-Qalam: 48]\nThe greatness of Yunus(as) is reduced with this and he was a prophet. So, Allah(swt) immediately says:\n﴿فَاجْتَبَاهُ رَبُّهُ فَجَعَلَهُ مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ ٥٠﴾\nAnd his Lord chose him and made him of the righteous.\n[Al-Qalam: 50]\nBecause Yunus(as) repented and exalted Allah(swt), he was from the righteous. Allah(swt) made the fish swallow Yunus(as) in order to warn him because it does not befit a prophet to do something without the command of Allah(swt). But this slip does not in any way decrease the greatness of Yunus(as). This is confirmed in the sahih hadith also in which the Holy Prophet(saws) says:\n“It is not proper for anyone to say that he is better than Yunus(as), son of Matta.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, Anbiya, 24,35; Sahih Muslim,166)\nWe come to know from the Bible that Yunus(as) came back to Nineveh and the people there accepted Christianity. He stayed with them and kept preaching to them till his death. Even today there is a grave there which people say is that of Yunus(as). Only Allah(swt) knows the truth about it.\nWe learn the following lessons from the story of Yunus(as):\n1. Exalting Allah(swt) and worshipping Allah(swt) is the only way out of troubles as Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿فَلَوْلَا أَنَّهُ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُسَبِّحِينَ ١٤٣ لَلَبِثَ فِي بَطْنِهِ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ ١٤٤﴾\nAnd had he not been of those who exalt Allah, He would have remained inside its belly until the Day they are resurrected.\n[As-Saffat: 143, 144]\nYunus(as) was a prophet of Allah(swt) who was always engrossed in the worship of Allah(swt). That is why when he was in trouble, Allah(swt) saved him.\n2. We should worship Allah(swt) alone when we are facing troubles or going through a bad phase in life and not invoke others. When Yunus(as) was in the belly of the fish, he prayed to Allah(swt) with the following supplication, which when recited with a pure and sincere heart and complete faith in Allah(swt) is sure to be accepted by Him:\nأَن لَّا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا أَنتَ سُبْحَانَكَ إِنِّي كُنتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ\n\"There is no deity except You; exalted are You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers.\"\n[Al-Anbiya: 87]\n3. When we face troubles while treading the path of Allah(swt), we must have patience. Allah(swt) says to the Holy Prophet(saws) that when he is having problems in the propagation of Islam, then he(saws) should have patience and not become impatient like the man of the fish namely Yunus(as). He(swt) asks him not to take any decision in haste but to wait for the command of Allah(swt) and not run away from troubles like Yunus(as). This incident is also a lesson for the people who are engaged in the ‘dawah’ work for the propagation of Islam."],[361,"§Yusuf(as)\nYusuf(as) was the great-grandson of Ibraheem(as) and the son of Yaqub(as). He was born in 1745 B. C. and died in 1635 B. C. His life has been described in great detail in the Holy Quran and his story has in fact been described as the best of stories. (See: Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-3) and a whole surah has been revealed in his name. Yusuf(as) has been described in the Bible also. Briefly his story is as follows:\nYaqub(as) had twelve sons and of them Yusuf and Benjamin were from Rachel, who died during the birth of Benjamin. While Yusuf(as) was still young he had a dream in which he saw the sun, moon and eleven stars prostrating in front of him. It is mentioned in the Holy Quran that he told about this dream only to his father Yaqub(as) and Yaqub(as) asked him not to tell about it to anyone:\n﴿قَالَ يَا بُنَيَّ لَا تَقْصُصْ رُؤْيَاكَ عَلَىٰ إِخْوَتِكَ فَيَكِيدُوا لَكَ كَيْدًا ۖ إِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ لِلْإِنسَانِ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِينٌ ٥﴾\nHe said, \"O my son, do not relate your vision to your brothers or they will contrive against you a plan. Indeed Satan, to man, is a manifest enemy.\n[Yusuf: 5]\nBut it is mentioned in the Bible that Yusuf(as) related his dream to his father as well as his brothers. (See: Genesis 37:5) But this is not true because due to the preference which Yaqub(as) gave to Yusuf(as), Yusuf(as) was hated by his brothers. And if he had told them about the dream, they would have become even more jealous and hated Yusuf(as) even more. Here the sun and the moon represent the father and mother of Yusuf(as) and the eleven stars represent his eleven brothers which included his step-brothers also. Yusuf(as) and Benjamin were from the same mother. The hatred of the brothers for Yusuf(as) is described in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿لَّقَدْ كَانَ فِي يُوسُفَ وَإِخْوَتِهِ آيَاتٌ لِّلسَّائِلِينَ ٧ إِذْ قَالُوا لَيُوسُفُ وَأَخُوهُ أَحَبُّ إِلَىٰ أَبِينَا مِنَّا وَنَحْنُ عُصْبَةٌ إِنَّ أَبَانَا لَفِي ضَلَالٍ مُّبِينٍ ٨ اقْتُلُوا يُوسُفَ أَوِ اطْرَحُوهُ أَرْضًا يَخْلُ لَكُمْ وَجْهُ أَبِيكُمْ وَتَكُونُوا مِن بَعْدِهِ قَوْمًا صَالِحِينَ ٩ قَالَ قَائِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ لَا تَقْتُلُوا يُوسُفَ وَأَلْقُوهُ فِي غَيَابَتِ الْجُبِّ يَلْتَقِطْهُ بَعْضُ السَّيَّارَةِ إِن كُنتُمْ فَاعِلِينَ ١٠﴾\nCertainly were there in Joseph and his brothers signs for those who ask, When they said, \"Joseph and his brother are more beloved to our father than we, while we are a clan. Indeed, our father is in clear error. Kill Joseph or cast him out to [another] land; the countenance of your father will [then] be only for you, and you will be after that a righteous people.\" Said a speaker among them, \"Do not kill Joseph but throw him into the bottom of the well; some travelers will pick him up - if you would do [something].\"\n[Yusuf: 7-10]\nIn the Bible, book of Genesis, it is mentioned that the brother who said this was Reuben. He wanted to rescue Yusuf(as) after his other brothers had left and take him back to his father. (Genesis 37/21)\nBut it appears that the brother who said this was his own brother Benjamin during whose birth, Yusuf(as)’s mother had died. For this reason Yaqub(as) was more affectionate to these two and this made the other brothers jealous.\nWhen they had thus decided that they would somehow take away Yusuf(as) and throw him into a well, they told their father Yaqub(as):\n﴿قَالُوا يَا أَبَانَا مَا لَكَ لَا تَأْمَنَّا عَلَىٰ يُوسُفَ وَإِنَّا لَهُ لَنَاصِحُونَ ١١ أَرْسِلْهُ مَعَنَا غَدًا يَرْتَعْ وَيَلْعَبْ وَإِنَّا لَهُ لَحَافِظُونَ ١٢ قَالَ إِنِّي لَيَحْزُنُنِي أَن تَذْهَبُوا بِهِ وَأَخَافُ أَن يَأْكُلَهُ الذِّئْبُ وَأَنتُمْ عَنْهُ غَافِلُونَ ١٣ قَالُوا لَئِنْ أَكَلَهُ الذِّئْبُ وَنَحْنُ عُصْبَةٌ إِنَّا إِذًا لَّخَاسِرُونَ ١٤﴾\nThey said, \"O our father, why do you not entrust us with Joseph while indeed, we are to him sincere counselors? Send him with us tomorrow that he may eat well and play. And indeed, we will be his guardians. [Jacob] said, \"Indeed, it saddens me that you should take him, and I fear that a wolf would eat him while you are of him unaware.\" They said, \"If a wolf should eat him while we are a [strong] clan, indeed, we would then be losers.\"\n[Yusuf: 11-14]\nWhen the brothers insisted thus, Yaqub(as) sent Yusuf(as) with them, but he was restless with worry lest something bad happen to Yusuf(as):\n﴿فَلَمَّا ذَهَبُوا بِهِ وَأَجْمَعُوا أَن يَجْعَلُوهُ فِي غَيَابَتِ الْجُبِّ ۚ وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْهِ لَتُنَبِّئَنَّهُم بِأَمْرِهِمْ هَـٰذَا وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ١٥﴾\nSo when they took him [out] and agreed to put him into the bottom of the well... But We inspired to him, \"You will surely inform them [someday] about this affair of theirs while they do not perceive [your identity].\"\n[Yusuf: 15]\nThere is a continuity in the way the story of Yusuf(as) is narrated in the Holy Quran. It is given in the Bible that Yaqub(as) himself sent Yusuf(as) after his brothers to see if all was well. When the brothers saw Yusuf(as) coming, they plotted to kill him. (See: Genesis 37:14-22). This does not seem true because when Yaqub(as) himself did not trust his other sons to look after Yusuf(as), it is not possible that he would’ve sent his favourite son in search of the brothers who hated him. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَجَاءُوا أَبَاهُمْ عِشَاءً يَبْكُونَ ١٦ قَالُوا يَا أَبَانَا إِنَّا ذَهَبْنَا نَسْتَبِقُ وَتَرَكْنَا يُوسُفَ عِندَ مَتَاعِنَا فَأَكَلَهُ الذِّئْبُ ۖ وَمَا أَنتَ بِمُؤْمِنٍ لَّنَا وَلَوْ كُنَّا صَادِقِينَ ١٧ وَجَاءُوا عَلَىٰ قَمِيصِهِ بِدَمٍ كَذِبٍ ۚ قَالَ بَلْ سَوَّلَتْ لَكُمْ أَنفُسُكُمْ أَمْرًا ۖ فَصَبْرٌ جَمِيلٌ ۖ وَاللَّـهُ الْمُسْتَعَانُ عَلَىٰ مَا تَصِفُونَ ١٨﴾\nAnd they came to their father at night, weeping. They said, \"O our father, indeed we went racing each other and left Joseph with our possessions, and a wolf ate him. But you would not believe us, even if we were truthful.\" And they brought upon his shirt false blood. [Jacob] said, \"Rather, your souls have enticed you to something, so patience is most fitting. And Allah is the one sought for help against that which you describe.\"\n[Yusuf: 16-18]\nIt is said that they slaughtered a sheep and applied the blood to the shirt of Yusuf(as) and took it to Yaqub(as). Yaqub(as) understood that it was a plot of the evil brothers because if a wolf had killed Yusuf(as), then his shirt would’ve been torn but it was not. And the story goes on:\n﴿وَجَاءَتْ سَيَّارَةٌ فَأَرْسَلُوا وَارِدَهُمْ فَأَدْلَىٰ دَلْوَهُ ۖ قَالَ يَا بُشْرَىٰ هَـٰذَا غُلَامٌ ۚ وَأَسَرُّوهُ بِضَاعَةً ۚ وَاللَّـهُ عَلِيمٌ بِمَا يَعْمَلُونَ ١٩﴾\nAnd there came a company of travelers; then they sent their water drawer, and he let down his bucket. He said, \"Good news! Here is a boy.\" And they concealed him, [taking him] as merchandise; and Allah was knowing of what they did.\n[Yusuf: 19]\nIn this story there is a hidden message. Allah(swt) is conveying to the Holy Prophet(saws) that just as the brothers of Yusuf(as) were forced to come to Yusuf(as) when he ascended the throne, the disbelievers of Makkah will be forced to accept their defeat; and exactly the same thing happened after the victory over Makkah.\nWhen the caravan of the travellers took out Yusuf(as) and took him with them, Yusuf(as)’s brothers followed them and told them that he was their servant and had got separated from them. But they wanted to sell him as they were fed up of him. The travellers bought him for a paltry sum of twenty Dirhams and the brothers shared the money – two Dirhams each. Judah, the eleventh brother did not take his share. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَشَرَوْهُ بِثَمَنٍ بَخْسٍ دَرَاهِمَ مَعْدُودَةٍ وَكَانُوا فِيهِ مِنَ الزَّاهِدِينَ ٢٠﴾\nAnd they sold him for a reduced price - a few dirhams - and they were, concerning him, of those content with little.\n[Yusuf: 20]\nWho were the people who sold Yusuf(as) – his brothers or the travellers? It is given in the book Genesis of the Bible that his brothers sold Yusuf(as) and then the travellers sold him to a person in Egypt. This person’s name is mentioned as Potiphar in the Bible who was a superintendent in Egypt. He is called ‘Aziz’ in the Holy Quran. This may have been his title that is: chief minister.\nThe other version is that the travelers took Yusuf(as) out of the well and took him to Egypt and sold him away for a small sum. But the question is why did they sell such an adorable boy for a paltry sum and why were they not attached to the boy when he was just seventeen? Therefore selling him for a small sum and not being attached to him applies to the brothers as they just wanted to get rid of Yusuf(as). This same view is held by Abdullah-bin-Abbas and the prominent commentator of the Holy Quran Ibn-Zareer-Tabri.\nOne other fantastic thing is mentioned in the Taurah that the travellers who took Yusuf(as) out of the well and sold him to the Egyptian were related to the family of Ismael(as) who were taking spices, oil and other commodities from Jil’ad to Egypt. But as everyone is aware the descendants of Ismael(as) inhabited Makkah and there are two routes from Makkah to Egypt. One is the sea-route from Jeddah and the other is through the desert of Sinai. And neither of these two routes goes through the place where Yusuf(as) was thrown into the well. That is, this place is Dosan near Shukaim in Syria and about nine miles from Samira. Then how did the Ismaelites reach this place?\nIt is clear from this that the dislike which the Bani-Israel had for Hajira and her son Ismael(as) in the beginning was still present and they displayed it whenever there was a chance. This is also the reason why the Bani-Israel (Jews) rejected Prophet Muhammad(saws) though they recognized him from the various signs, just because he(saws) was from Bani-Ismael.\nThen, the story goes that Yusuf(as) was bought by the Egyptian Aziz or the chief minister named Potiphar. His wife was named Zulekha or Rachel (but none of these names is mentioned in the Taurah; it is possible that they are mentioned in the Israeli scriptures). She was attracted to Yusuf(as) and tried to seduce him in various ways. One day she bolted the door from inside and Yusuf(as) got scared and started running away. She managed to take hold of his shirt and it got torn. Then she complained to the Aziz and accused Yusuf(as). Aziz was taken in by the lies of his wife. In the end one person said that if the shirt is torn in the front then Yusuf(as) was guilty and if it is torn at the back then the woman was guilty. Aziz saw that the shirt was torn at the back and was convinced that Yusuf(as) was innocent and that his wife was the liar. This news spread everywhere that the wife of Aziz was attracted to her servant. The women of the town started slandering the wife of Aziz. One day the wife of Aziz invited the prominent ladies of the town to a feast. She kept a knife before each of them for cutting the fruits and eating them. Then she asked Yusuf(as) to come out before them. On seeing Yusuf(as) they were lost in a trance and cut their hands and exclaimed that this was no human but an angel. Then the wife of Aziz said that this was the same servant about whom they were saying all sorts of things. When they could get so lost in his beauty that they ended up cutting themselves, why were they blaming her for being attracted to him? She said that she had tried many ways of seducing him, but he had eluded her. So, she finally asked Yusuf(as) to agree to her request or face imprisonment and dishonor. Yusuf(as) called out to Allah(swt):\n﴿قَالَ رَبِّ السِّجْنُ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ مِمَّا يَدْعُونَنِي إِلَيْهِ ۖ وَإِلَّا تَصْرِفْ عَنِّي كَيْدَهُنَّ أَصْبُ إِلَيْهِنَّ وَأَكُن مِّنَ الْجَاهِلِينَ ٣٣﴾\n\"My Lord, prison is more to my liking than that to which they invite me. And if You do not avert from me their plan, I might incline toward them and [thus] be of the ignorant.\"\n[Yusuf: 33]\nAllah(swt) heard Yusuf(as)’s prayer and saved him from those evil ladies. Aziz and his relatives had Yusuf(as) imprisoned. The prison proved a good place for Yusuf(as) to spread the message of Allah(swt). There he started inviting people towards ‘Tawheed’ as Ibraheem(as), Ishaq(as) and Yaqub(as) had before him. And along with this he also started interpreting the dreams of people. One prisoner dreamt that he was pressing wine and another dreamt that he was carrying bread on his head which the birds were pecking. Both of them asked Yusuf(as) the interpretation of their dreams. First Yusuf(as) gave them the message of One God and forbade them from shirk and polytheism which was also preached by all the other prophets and then addressed them:\nيَا صَاحِبَيِ السِّجْنِ أَأَرْبَابٌ مُّتَفَرِّقُونَ خَيْرٌ أَمِ اللَّهُ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُ\nO [my] two companions of prison, are separate lords better or Allah, the One, the Prevailing?\n[Yusuf: 39]\nIt is obvious that it is best to believe in One Allah(swt) rather than multiple gods and goddesses. Then he said,\nمَا تَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِهِ إِلَّا أَسْمَاءً سَمَّيْتُمُوهَا أَنتُمْ وَآبَاؤُكُم مَّا أَنزَلَ اللَّهُ بِهَا مِن سُلْطَانٍ ۚ إِنِ الْحُكْمُ إِلَّا لِلَّهِ ۚ أَمَرَ أَلَّا تَعْبُدُوا إِلَّا إِيَّاهُ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ الدِّينُ الْقَيِّمُ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ\nYou worship not besides Him except [mere] names you have named them, you and your fathers, for which Allah has sent down no authority. Legislation is not but for Allah. He has commanded that you worship not except Him. That is the correct religion, but most of the people do not know.\n[Yusuf: 40]\nThen Yusuf(as) explained the meaning of their dreams. The person who was pressing wine would be freed and serve wine to his master and the other one who was carrying bread would be hanged. It happened as foretold. But Yusuf(as) had to stay in prison for many more years as the prisoner who was released forgot to tell the king what Yusuf(as) had told him. One night the king saw a strange dream in which seven lean cows were eating seven fat cows and there were seven green spikes of grain and seven dry ones. The king asked all his courtiers the meaning of this dream but they could not interpret it. Now, the person who was serving wine to the king remembered about Yusuf(as) and said that he could interpret the dream if he was taken to Yusuf(as). The rest of the story in the Holy Quran is as follows:\n﴿يُوسُفُ أَيُّهَا الصِّدِّيقُ أَفْتِنَا فِي سَبْعِ بَقَرَاتٍ سِمَانٍ يَأْكُلُهُنَّ سَبْعٌ عِجَافٌ وَسَبْعِ سُنبُلَاتٍ خُضْرٍ وَأُخَرَ يَابِسَاتٍ لَّعَلِّي أَرْجِعُ إِلَى النَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ ٤٦ قَالَ تَزْرَعُونَ سَبْعَ سِنِينَ دَأَبًا فَمَا حَصَدتُّمْ فَذَرُوهُ فِي سُنبُلِهِ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِّمَّا تَأْكُلُونَ ٤٧ ثُمَّ يَأْتِي مِن بَعْدِ ذَٰلِكَ سَبْعٌ شِدَادٌ يَأْكُلْنَ مَا قَدَّمْتُمْ لَهُنَّ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِّمَّا تُحْصِنُونَ ٤٨ ثُمَّ يَأْتِي مِن بَعْدِ ذَٰلِكَ عَامٌ فِيهِ يُغَاثُ النَّاسُ وَفِيهِ يَعْصِرُونَ ٤٩ وَقَالَ الْمَلِكُ ائْتُونِي بِهِ ۖ فَلَمَّا جَاءَهُ الرَّسُولُ قَالَ ارْجِعْ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ فَاسْأَلْهُ مَا بَالُ النِّسْوَةِ اللَّاتِي قَطَّعْنَ أَيْدِيَهُنَّ ۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي بِكَيْدِهِنَّ عَلِيمٌ ٥٠ قَالَ مَا خَطْبُكُنَّ إِذْ رَاوَدتُّنَّ يُوسُفَ عَن نَّفْسِهِ ۚ قُلْنَ حَاشَ لِلَّهِ مَا عَلِمْنَا عَلَيْهِ مِن سُوءٍ ۚ قَالَتِ امْرَأَتُ الْعَزِيزِ الْآنَ حَصْحَصَ الْحَقُّ أَنَا رَاوَدتُّهُ عَن نَّفْسِهِ وَإِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ ٥١ ذَٰلِكَ لِيَعْلَمَ أَنِّي لَمْ أَخُنْهُ بِالْغَيْبِ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَهْدِي كَيْدَ الْخَائِنِينَ ٥٢ (13) ۞ وَمَا أُبَرِّئُ نَفْسِي ۚ إِنَّ النَّفْسَ لَأَمَّارَةٌ بِالسُّوءِ إِلَّا مَا رَحِمَ رَبِّي ۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ٥٣ وَقَالَ الْمَلِكُ ائْتُونِي بِهِ أَسْتَخْلِصْهُ لِنَفْسِي ۖ فَلَمَّا كَلَّمَهُ قَالَ إِنَّكَ الْيَوْمَ لَدَيْنَا مَكِينٌ أَمِينٌ ٥٤ قَالَ اجْعَلْنِي عَلَىٰ خَزَائِنِ الْأَرْضِ ۖ إِنِّي حَفِيظٌ عَلِيمٌ ٥٥ وَكَذَٰلِكَ مَكَّنَّا لِيُوسُفَ فِي الْأَرْضِ يَتَبَوَّأُ مِنْهَا حَيْثُ يَشَاءُ ۚ نُصِيبُ بِرَحْمَتِنَا مَن نَّشَاءُ ۖ وَلَا نُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِينَ ٥٦ وَلَأَجْرُ الْآخِرَةِ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَكَانُوا يَتَّقُونَ ٥٧﴾\n[He said], \"Joseph, O man of truth, explain to us about seven fat cows eaten by seven [that were] lean, and seven green spikes [of grain] and others [that were] dry - that I may return to the people; perhaps they will know [about you].\" [Joseph] said, \"You will plant for seven years consecutively; and what you harvest leave in its spikes, except a little from which you will eat. Then will come after that seven difficult [years] which will consume what you saved for them, except a little from which you will store. Then will come after that a year in which the people will be given rain and in which they will press [olives and grapes].\" And the king said, \"Bring him to me.\" But when the messenger came to him, [Joseph] said, \"Return to your master and ask him what is the case of the women who cut their hands. Indeed, my Lord is Knowing of their plan.\" Said [the king to the women], \"What was your condition when you sought to seduce Joseph?\" They said, \"Perfect is Allah! We know about him no evil.\" The wife of al-'Azeez said, \"Now the truth has become evident. It was I who sought to seduce him, and indeed, he is of the truthful. That is so al-'Azeez will know that I did not betray him in [his] absence and that Allah does not guide the plan of betrayers. And I do not acquit myself. Indeed, the soul is a persistent enjoiner of evil, except those upon which my Lord has mercy. Indeed, my Lord is Forgiving and Merciful.\" And the king said, \"Bring him to me; I will appoint him exclusively for myself.\" And when he spoke to him, he said, \"Indeed, you are today established [in position] and trusted.\" [Joseph] said, \"Appoint me over the storehouses of the land. Indeed, I will be a knowing guardian.\" And thus We established Joseph in the land to settle therein wherever he willed. We touch with Our mercy whom We will, and We do not allow to be lost the reward of those who do good. And the reward of the Hereafter is better for those who believed and were fearing Allah.\n[Yusuf: 46-57]\nAccording to the Bible, Yusuf(as) was thirty years old by this time. Out of these thirteen years had been very difficult ones. The king also got him married. His wife was Asenath, the daughter of the priest of On. He had two sons: Manasseh and Ephraim. (See: Genesis: 41/51)\nNow Yusuf(as) started living in Egypt in great comfort. He was the most powerful man after the king. In this way, the boy who was thrown into a well by his brothers was in the seat of the special minister to the king of Egypt. He became known far and wide for his justice. The famine which had afflicted Egypt passed and it started progressing rapidly. Then there was a drought in Syria and Palestine and people from these places started coming to Egypt as the king there was kind and just. Among them were Yusuf(as)’s brothers too. Yusuf(as) recognised them but did not let them know about him. He enquired about his parents and other brothers and got all the information about his home. When they were going back, Yusuf(as) asked them to bring Benjamin with them when they came back or else he said that he would not give them anything. (See: Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verses-59-61)\nWhen they reached Palestine they asked Yaqub(as) to send brother Benjamin with them as Yusuf(as) had asked them to. But Yaqub(as) was unwilling as they had already lost his favourite Yusuf(as). But he finally agreed when the brothers were very insistent. When they were leaving, Yaqub(as) gave them some useful advice which is mentioned in the Holy Quran as:\n﴿وَقَالَ يَا بَنِيَّ لَا تَدْخُلُوا مِن بَابٍ وَاحِدٍ وَادْخُلُوا مِنْ أَبْوَابٍ مُّتَفَرِّقَةٍ ۖ وَمَا أُغْنِي عَنكُم مِّنَ اللَّـهِ مِن شَيْءٍ ۖ إِنِ الْحُكْمُ إِلَّا لِلَّـهِ ۖ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ ۖ وَعَلَيْهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُتَوَكِّلُونَ ٦٧ وَلَمَّا دَخَلُوا مِنْ حَيْثُ أَمَرَهُمْ أَبُوهُم مَّا كَانَ يُغْنِي عَنْهُم مِّنَ اللَّـهِ مِن شَيْءٍ إِلَّا حَاجَةً فِي نَفْسِ يَعْقُوبَ قَضَاهَا ۚ وَإِنَّهُ لَذُو عِلْمٍ لِّمَا عَلَّمْنَاهُ وَلَـٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ٦٨ وَلَمَّا دَخَلُوا عَلَىٰ يُوسُفَ آوَىٰ إِلَيْهِ أَخَاهُ ۖ قَالَ إِنِّي أَنَا أَخُوكَ فَلَا تَبْتَئِسْ بِمَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ ٦٩ فَلَمَّا جَهَّزَهُم بِجَهَازِهِمْ جَعَلَ السِّقَايَةَ فِي رَحْلِ أَخِيهِ ثُمَّ أَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ أَيَّتُهَا الْعِيرُ إِنَّكُمْ لَسَارِقُونَ ٧٠ قَالُوا وَأَقْبَلُوا عَلَيْهِم مَّاذَا تَفْقِدُونَ ٧١ قَالُوا نَفْقِدُ صُوَاعَ الْمَلِكِ وَلِمَن جَاءَ بِهِ حِمْلُ بَعِيرٍ وَأَنَا بِهِ زَعِيمٌ ٧٢ قَالُوا تَاللَّـهِ لَقَدْ عَلِمْتُم مَّا جِئْنَا لِنُفْسِدَ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَمَا كُنَّا سَارِقِينَ ٧٣ قَالُوا فَمَا جَزَاؤُهُ إِن كُنتُمْ كَاذِبِينَ ٧٤ قَالُوا جَزَاؤُهُ مَن وُجِدَ فِي رَحْلِهِ فَهُوَ جَزَاؤُهُ ۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِي الظَّالِمِينَ ٧٥ فَبَدَأَ بِأَوْعِيَتِهِمْ قَبْلَ وِعَاءِ أَخِيهِ ثُمَّ اسْتَخْرَجَهَا مِن وِعَاءِ أَخِيهِ ۚ كَذَٰلِكَ كِدْنَا لِيُوسُفَ ۖ مَا كَانَ لِيَأْخُذَ أَخَاهُ فِي دِينِ الْمَلِكِ إِلَّا أَن يَشَاءَ اللَّـهُ ۚ نَرْفَعُ دَرَجَاتٍ مَّن نَّشَاءُ ۗ وَفَوْقَ كُلِّ ذِي عِلْمٍ عَلِيمٌ ٧٦ قَالُوا إِن يَسْرِقْ فَقَدْ سَرَقَ أَخٌ لَّهُ مِن قَبْلُ ۚ فَأَسَرَّهَا يُوسُفُ فِي نَفْسِهِ وَلَمْ يُبْدِهَا لَهُمْ ۚ قَالَ أَنتُمْ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا ۖ وَاللَّـهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَصِفُونَ ٧٧ قَالُوا يَا أَيُّهَا الْعَزِيزُ إِنَّ لَهُ أَبًا شَيْخًا كَبِيرًا فَخُذْ أَحَدَنَا مَكَانَهُ ۖ إِنَّا نَرَاكَ مِنَ الْمُحْسِنِينَ ٧٨ قَالَ مَعَاذَ اللَّـهِ أَن نَّأْخُذَ إِلَّا مَن وَجَدْنَا مَتَاعَنَا عِندَهُ إِنَّا إِذًا لَّظَالِمُونَ ٧٩ فَلَمَّا اسْتَيْأَسُوا مِنْهُ خَلَصُوا نَجِيًّا ۖ قَالَ كَبِيرُهُمْ أَلَمْ تَعْلَمُوا أَنَّ أَبَاكُمْ قَدْ أَخَذَ عَلَيْكُم مَّوْثِقًا مِّنَ اللَّـهِ وَمِن قَبْلُ مَا فَرَّطتُمْ فِي يُوسُفَ ۖ فَلَنْ أَبْرَحَ الْأَرْضَ حَتَّىٰ يَأْذَنَ لِي أَبِي أَوْ يَحْكُمَ اللَّـهُ لِي ۖ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الْحَاكِمِينَ ٨٠ ارْجِعُوا إِلَىٰ أَبِيكُمْ فَقُولُوا يَا أَبَانَا إِنَّ ابْنَكَ سَرَقَ وَمَا شَهِدْنَا إِلَّا بِمَا عَلِمْنَا وَمَا كُنَّا لِلْغَيْبِ حَافِظِينَ ٨١ وَاسْأَلِ الْقَرْيَةَ الَّتِي كُنَّا فِيهَا وَالْعِيرَ الَّتِي أَقْبَلْنَا فِيهَا ۖ وَإِنَّا لَصَادِقُونَ ٨٢ قَالَ بَلْ سَوَّلَتْ لَكُمْ أَنفُسُكُمْ أَمْرًا ۖ فَصَبْرٌ جَمِيلٌ ۖ عَسَى اللَّـهُ أَن يَأْتِيَنِي بِهِمْ جَمِيعًا ۚ إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْعَلِيمُ الْحَكِيمُ ٨٣ وَتَوَلَّىٰ عَنْهُمْ وَقَالَ يَا أَسَفَىٰ عَلَىٰ يُوسُفَ وَابْيَضَّتْ عَيْنَاهُ مِنَ الْحُزْنِ فَهُوَ كَظِيمٌ ٨٤ قَالُوا تَاللَّـهِ تَفْتَأُ تَذْكُرُ يُوسُفَ حَتَّىٰ تَكُونَ حَرَضًا أَوْ تَكُونَ مِنَ الْهَالِكِينَ ٨٥ قَالَ إِنَّمَا أَشْكُو بَثِّي وَحُزْنِي إِلَى اللَّـهِ وَأَعْلَمُ مِنَ اللَّـهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ ٨٦ يَا بَنِيَّ اذْهَبُوا فَتَحَسَّسُوا مِن يُوسُفَ وَأَخِيهِ وَلَا تَيْأَسُوا مِن رَّوْحِ اللَّـهِ ۖ إِنَّهُ لَا يَيْأَسُ مِن رَّوْحِ اللَّـهِ إِلَّا الْقَوْمُ الْكَافِرُونَ ٨٧ فَلَمَّا دَخَلُوا عَلَيْهِ قَالُوا يَا أَيُّهَا الْعَزِيزُ مَسَّنَا وَأَهْلَنَا الضُّرُّ وَجِئْنَا بِبِضَاعَةٍ مُّزْجَاةٍ فَأَوْفِ لَنَا الْكَيْلَ وَتَصَدَّقْ عَلَيْنَا ۖ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَجْزِي الْمُتَصَدِّقِينَ ٨٨ قَالَ هَلْ عَلِمْتُم مَّا فَعَلْتُم بِيُوسُفَ وَأَخِيهِ إِذْ أَنتُمْ جَاهِلُونَ ٨٩ قَالُوا أَإِنَّكَ لَأَنتَ يُوسُفُ ۖ قَالَ أَنَا يُوسُفُ وَهَـٰذَا أَخِي ۖ قَدْ مَنَّ اللَّـهُ عَلَيْنَا ۖ إِنَّهُ مَن يَتَّقِ وَيَصْبِرْ فَإِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَا يُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِينَ ٩٠ قَالُوا تَاللَّـهِ لَقَدْ آثَرَكَ اللَّـهُ عَلَيْنَا وَإِن كُنَّا لَخَاطِئِينَ ٩١ قَالَ لَا تَثْرِيبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْيَوْمَ ۖ يَغْفِرُ اللَّـهُ لَكُمْ ۖ وَهُوَ أَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِينَ ٩٢ اذْهَبُوا بِقَمِيصِي هَـٰذَا فَأَلْقُوهُ عَلَىٰ وَجْهِ أَبِي يَأْتِ بَصِيرًا وَأْتُونِي بِأَهْلِكُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ ٩٣ وَلَمَّا فَصَلَتِ الْعِيرُ قَالَ أَبُوهُمْ إِنِّي لَأَجِدُ رِيحَ يُوسُفَ ۖ لَوْلَا أَن تُفَنِّدُونِ ٩٤ قَالُوا تَاللَّـهِ إِنَّكَ لَفِي ضَلَالِكَ الْقَدِيمِ ٩٥ فَلَمَّا أَن جَاءَ الْبَشِيرُ أَلْقَاهُ عَلَىٰ وَجْهِهِ فَارْتَدَّ بَصِيرًا ۖ قَالَ أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ مِنَ اللَّـهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ ٩٦ قَالُوا يَا أَبَانَا اسْتَغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَا إِنَّا كُنَّا خَاطِئِينَ ٩٧ قَالَ سَوْفَ أَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكُمْ رَبِّي ۖ إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْغَفُورُ الرَّحِيمُ ٩٨ فَلَمَّا دَخَلُوا عَلَىٰ يُوسُفَ آوَىٰ إِلَيْهِ أَبَوَيْهِ وَقَالَ ادْخُلُوا مِصْرَ إِن شَاءَ اللَّـهُ آمِنِينَ ٩٩ وَرَفَعَ أَبَوَيْهِ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ وَخَرُّوا لَهُ سُجَّدًا ۖ وَقَالَ يَا أَبَتِ هَـٰذَا تَأْوِيلُ رُؤْيَايَ مِن قَبْلُ قَدْ جَعَلَهَا رَبِّي حَقًّا ۖ وَقَدْ أَحْسَنَ بِي إِذْ أَخْرَجَنِي مِنَ السِّجْنِ وَجَاءَ بِكُم مِّنَ الْبَدْوِ مِن بَعْدِ أَن نَّزَغَ الشَّيْطَانُ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَ إِخْوَتِي ۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي لَطِيفٌ لِّمَا يَشَاءُ ۚ إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْعَلِيمُ الْحَكِيمُ ١٠٠ رَبِّ قَدْ آتَيْتَنِي مِنَ الْمُلْكِ وَعَلَّمْتَنِي مِن تَأْوِيلِ الْأَحَادِيثِ ۚ فَاطِرَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ أَنتَ وَلِيِّي فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ ۖ تَوَفَّنِي مُسْلِمًا وَأَلْحِقْنِي بِالصَّالِحِينَ ١٠١ ذَٰلِكَ مِنْ أَنبَاءِ الْغَيْبِ نُوحِيهِ إِلَيْكَ ۖ وَمَا كُنتَ لَدَيْهِمْ إِذْ أَجْمَعُوا أَمْرَهُمْ وَهُمْ يَمْكُرُونَ ١٠٢﴾\nAnd he said, \"O my sons, do not enter from one gate but enter from different gates; and I cannot avail you against [the decree of] Allah at all. The decision is only for Allah; upon Him I have relied, and upon Him let those who would rely [indeed] rely.\" And when they entered from where their father had ordered them, it did not avail them against Allah at all except [it was] a need within the soul of Jacob, which he satisfied. And indeed, he was a possessor of knowledge because of what We had taught him, but most of the people do not know. And when they entered upon Joseph, he took his brother to himself; he said, \"Indeed, I am your brother, so do not despair over what they used to do [to me].\" So when he had furnished them with their supplies, he put the [gold measuring] bowl into the bag of his brother. Then an announcer called out, \"O caravan, indeed you are thieves.\" They said while approaching them, \"What is it you are missing?\" They said, \"We are missing the measure of the king. And for he who produces it is [the reward of] a camel's load, and I am responsible for it.\" They said, \"By Allah, you have certainly known that we did not come to cause corruption in the land, and we have not been thieves.\" The accusers said, \"Then what would be its recompense if you should be liars?\"[The brothers] said, \"Its recompense is that he in whose bag it is found - he [himself] will be its recompense. Thus do we recompense the wrongdoers.\" So he began [the search] with their bags before the bag of his brother; then he extracted it from the bag of his brother. Thus did We plan for Joseph. He could not have taken his brother within the religion of the king except that Allah willed. We raise in degrees whom We will, but over every possessor of knowledge is one [more] knowing. They said, \"If he steals - a brother of his has stolen before.\" But Joseph kept it within himself and did not reveal it to them. He said, \"You are worse in position, and Allah is most knowing of what you describe.\" They said, \"O 'Azeez, indeed he has a father [who is] an old man, so take one of us in place of him. Indeed, we see you as a doer of good.\" He said, \"[I seek] the refuge of Allah [to prevent] that we take except him with whom we found our possession. Indeed, we would then be unjust.\" So when they had despaired of him, they secluded themselves in private consultation. The eldest of them said, \"Do you not know that your father has taken upon you an oath by Allah and [that] before you failed in [your duty to] Joseph? So I will never leave [this] land until my father permits me or Allah decides for me, and He is the best of judges. Return to your father and say, \"O our father, indeed your son has stolen, and we did not testify except to what we knew. And we were not witnesses of the unseen, And ask the city in which we were and the caravan in which we came - and indeed, we are truthful,\" [Jacob] said, \"Rather, your souls have enticed you to something, so patience is most fitting. Perhaps Allah will bring them to me all together. Indeed it is He who is the Knowing, the Wise.\" And he turned away from them and said, \"Oh, my sorrow over Joseph,\" and his eyes became white from grief, for he was [of that] a suppressor. They said, \"By Allah, you will not cease remembering Joseph until you become fatally ill or become of those who perish.\" He said, \"I only complain of my suffering and my grief to Allah, and I know from Allah that which you do not know. O my sons, go and find out about Joseph and his brother and despair not of relief from Allah. Indeed, no one despairs of relief from Allah except the disbelieving people.\" So when they entered upon Joseph, they said, \"O 'Azeez, adversity has touched us and our family, and we have come with goods poor in quality, but give us full measure and be charitable to us. Indeed, Allah rewards the charitable.\" He said, \"Do you know what you did with Joseph and his brother when you were ignorant?\" They said, \"Are you indeed Joseph?\" He said \"I am Joseph, and this is my brother. Allah has certainly favored us. Indeed, he who fears Allah and is patient, then indeed, Allah does not allow to be lost the reward of those who do good.\" They said, \"By Allah, certainly has Allah preferred you over us, and indeed, we have been sinners.\" He said, \"No blame will there be upon you today. Allah will forgive you; and He is the most merciful of the merciful.\" Take this, my shirt, and cast it over the face of my father; he will become seeing. And bring me your family, all together.\" And when the caravan departed [from Egypt], their father said, \"Indeed, I find the smell of Joseph [and would say that he was alive] if you did not think me weakened in mind.\" They said, \"By Allah, indeed you are in your [same] old error.\" And when the bearer of good tidings arrived, he cast it over his face, and he returned [once again] seeing. He said, \"Did I not tell you that I know from Allah that which you do not know?\" They said, \"O our father, ask for us forgiveness of our sins; indeed, we have been sinners.\" He said, \"I will ask forgiveness for you from my Lord. Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\" And when they entered upon Joseph, he took his parents to himself and said, \"Enter Egypt, Allah willing, safe [and secure].\" And he raised his parents upon the throne, and they bowed to him in prostration. And he said, \"O my father, this is the explanation of my vision of before. My Lord has made it reality. And He was certainly good to me when He took me out of prison and brought you [here] from bedouin life after Satan had induced [estrangement] between me and my brothers. Indeed, my Lord is Subtle in what He wills. Indeed, it is He who is the Knowing, the Wise. My Lord, You have given me [something] of sovereignty and taught me of the interpretation of dreams. Creator of the heavens and earth, You are my protector in this world and in the Hereafter. Cause me to die a Muslim and join me with the righteous.\" That is from the news of the unseen which We reveal, [O Muhammad], to you. And you were not with them when they put together their plan while they conspired.\n[Yusuf: 67-102]\nAll this which has been mentioned in the Holy Quran was through divine revelations because the Holy Prophet(saws) could neither read so that he could tell the story of Yusuf(as) after reading it from somewhere; nor was he(saws) present when all these events occurred. In fact the plots and conspiracies were unknown to those who were not part of them. This is clear and indisputable proof of the prophethood of Muhammad(saws) and it establishes the fact beyond doubt that the Holy Quran is from Allah(swt).\nIn this way, due to Yusuf(as), the descendants of Yaqub(as) settled down in Egypt where they prospered. Then they had to move out of there.\nAccording to the Bible, when Yusuf(as) was a hundred years old, he passed away. According to the Egyptian custom, his body was mummified. When the Bani-Israel came out of Egypt, they brought the coffin of Yusuf(as) along with them and buried it in Shechem. (See: Genesis 50:26 and Joshua 24:32)\nThere is no doubt that Allah(swt) sent Yusuf(as) as His prophet. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ جَاءَكُمْ يُوسُفُ مِن قَبْلُ بِالْبَيِّنَاتِ فَمَا زِلْتُمْ فِي شَكٍّ مِّمَّا جَاءَكُم بِهِ ۖ حَتَّىٰ إِذَا هَلَكَ قُلْتُمْ لَن يَبْعَثَ اللَّـهُ مِن بَعْدِهِ رَسُولًا ۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللَّـهُ مَنْ هُوَ مُسْرِفٌ مُّرْتَابٌ ٣٤﴾\nAnd Joseph had already come to you before with clear proofs, but you remained in doubt of that which he brought to you, until when he died, you said, 'Never will Allah send a messenger after him.' Thus does Allah leave astray he who is a transgressor and skeptic.\"\n[Al-Momin: 34]\nThe message of Yusuf(as) was the same as that of the other prophets. The message is that there is only one God Allah(swt), He(swt) has created everything and therefore He(swt) alone is worthy of worship, no one else can be or should be worshipped. And whatever else the people worship are their own creations whom they call by various names; so how can they be worshipped? (See: Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verses-37-40)"],[362,"§Zabah (slaughter)\nSlaughtering an animal in a specific way (Islamic way) is called ‘Zabah’.\nIt is a must to take the name of Allah(swt) while slaughtering an animal. If it is slaughtered in someone else’s name, it becomes haraam (forbidden). (See: Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-173)\nIn the same way if an animal is slaughtered at the altar of some god or goddess or at some grave, then it becomes haraam (forbidden). [Al-Ma’ida: 3]\nIn the same verse of Surah-Ma’ida, even those animals have been forbidden which have died due to suffocation, or due to some injury, or by falling from a height, or by being gored except those which have been caught alive and then slaughtered in the name of Allah(swt)."],[363,"§Zaid\nHis full name was Zaid-bin-Haritha-bin-Sharaheel Al-Kalbi. He was actually from the Arab tribe but someone had sold him away as a slave. Khadija(ra) bought him and presented him to the Holy Prophet(saws). The Holy Prophet(saws) set him free and adopted him. This is described in Surah-33, Al-Ahzab, Verse-37 of the Holy Quran. He is also counted among the prominent companions of the Holy Prophet(saws). For more information see ‘Sahaba’."],[364,"§Zaitoon\n‘Zaitoon’ means olives. Its tree is found mostly in Syria and Palestine. Its leaves are green at the top and silvery on the bottom. It is a beautiful sight when the leaves flutter in the wind. Olives are useful in many ways. The fruits can be eaten with bread and olive oil is used for cooking. By filling the leaves of olives with rice, a special dish is prepared. That is, all the parts of the tree are useful. Olives are discussed at various places in the Bible also. When there was the Great Flood during the time of Nuh(as) and he and the believers were safely in the ark, Nuh(as) sends out a dove to see if the storm had ended. The dove comes back with an olive leaf and Nuh(as) comes to know that the storm has ended."],[365,"§Zakaria(as)\nZakaria(as) was a great prophet.\nHe was from the family of Ibraheem(as).\nHe was born in Palestine. He did carpentry to earn his living and spent his spare time serving in Masjid-e-Aqsa. He preached the message of Allah(swt) to the people coming there and encouraged them to offer namaz. He was the husband of the maternal aunt of Maryam. When Maryam’s mother offered her for service in Masjid-e-Aqsa, Zakaria became her guardian. It is mentioned elsewhere that he wasn’t Maryam’s uncle but her brother-in-law; that is, his wife was the sister of Maryam. When Zakaria was an old man of ninety, Yahya(as) was born to his wife who was barren and this was a miracle from Allah(swt). When Yahya(as) was thirty years old, he and Zakaria(as) were killed by Herod Antipas. That is why in one hadith Yahya(as) is described as Shahid Ibn-Shahid.\nIn Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-40 of the Holy Quran, the wife of Zakaria(as) is described as being barren. So, when the good news of a son is given to her she is very surprised as to how she, a barren woman can give birth to a son. Her name was Elizabeth or Elisheba, in Greek it is Elisavet and in Hebrew it is Elisheva. She was from the family of Haroon(as) and was the sister of Hanna, the mother of Maryam. That is why when a guardian was needed for Maryam, Zakaria was chosen as he was Maryam’s uncle. A detailed description of Elizabeth is given in the book Luke (1:5-24) of the Injeel.\nThe conclusions which we can draw from the Holy Quran are:\n1. He was very righteous:\n﴿وَزَكَرِيَّا وَيَحْيَىٰ وَعِيسَىٰ وَإِلْيَاسَ ۖ كُلٌّ مِّنَ الصَّالِحِينَ ٨٥﴾\nAnd Zechariah and John and Jesus and Elias - and all were of the righteous.\n[Al-An’am: 85]\n2. He was the Imam of Masjid-e-Aqsa:\nفَنَادَتْهُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ وَهُوَ قَائِمٌ يُصَلِّي فِي الْمِحْرَابِ\nSo the angels called him while he was standing in prayer in the chamber.\n[Al-i-Imran: 39]\nWhen Maryam’s mother gave her over for service in Masjid-e-Aqsa, then Zakaria became her guardian. The Holy Quran says:\nوَكَفَّلَهَا زَكَرِيَّا\nAnd put her in the care of Zechariah.\n[Al-i-Imran: 37]\n3. When he was old he prayed to Allah(swt) for a son and Allah(swt) accepted his prayer:\n﴿هُنَالِكَ دَعَا زَكَرِيَّا رَبَّهُ ۖ قَالَ رَبِّ هَبْ لِي مِن لَّدُنكَ ذُرِّيَّةً طَيِّبَةً ۖ إِنَّكَ سَمِيعُ الدُّعَاءِ ٣٨ فَنَادَتْهُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ وَهُوَ قَائِمٌ يُصَلِّي فِي الْمِحْرَابِ أَنَّ اللَّـهَ يُبَشِّرُكَ بِيَحْيَىٰ مُصَدِّقًا بِكَلِمَةٍ مِّنَ اللَّـهِ وَسَيِّدًا وَحَصُورًا وَنَبِيًّا مِّنَ الصَّالِحِينَ ٣٩﴾\nAt that, Zechariah called upon his Lord, saying, \"My Lord, grant me from Yourself a good offspring. Indeed, You are the Hearer of supplication.\" So the angels called him while he was standing in prayer in the chamber, \"Indeed, Allah gives you good tidings of John, confirming a word from Allah and [who will be] honorable, abstaining [from women], and a prophet from among the righteous.\"\n[Al-i-Imran: 38, 39]\n﴿يَا زَكَرِيَّا إِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلَامٍ اسْمُهُ يَحْيَىٰ لَمْ نَجْعَل لَّهُ مِن قَبْلُ سَمِيًّا ٧﴾\n[He was told], \"O Zechariah, indeed We give you good tidings of a boy whose name will be John. We have not assigned to any before [this] name.\"\n[Maryam: 7]\nفَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهُ وَوَهَبْنَا لَهُ يَحْيَىٰ\nSo We responded to him, and We gave to him John.\n[Al-Anbiya: 90]\n4. He preached the worship of Allah(swt) and asked people to extol the Greatness of Allah(swt):\n﴿فَخَرَجَ عَلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ مِنَ الْمِحْرَابِ فَأَوْحَىٰ إِلَيْهِمْ أَن سَبِّحُوا بُكْرَةً وَعَشِيًّا ١١﴾\nSo he came out to his people from the prayer chamber and signaled to them to exalt [Allah] in the morning and afternoon.\n[Maryam: 11]\nZakaria(as) preached what all the other prophets had preached: to worship the One True God Allah(swt), not to attribute partners to Him and to keep away from all forms of idolatry."],[366,"§Zakat\nThis is an Arabic word. This is a special form of charity. Its implicit meaning is both ‘to increase’ and ‘to purify’. That is, on giving zakat, the wealth does not decrease but increases; but we cannot perceive it. And moreover on giving zakat, our wealth is purified because our wealth includes the share of the orphans, needy and other poor people. The only way to purify our wealth is by giving zakat. It is narrated in the sahih hadith in this regard:\n“Wealth will be taken from the rich and distributed among the poor.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1395 and Sahih Muslim,29)\nIn the Holy Quran, the Holy Prophet(saws) has been commanded:\n﴿خُذْ مِنْ أَمْوَالِهِمْ صَدَقَةً تُطَهِّرُهُمْ وَتُزَكِّيهِم بِهَا وَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِمْ ۖ إِنَّ صَلَاتَكَ سَكَنٌ لَّهُمْ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ ١٠٣﴾\nTake, [O, Muhammad], from their wealth a charity by which you purify them and cause them increase, and invoke [Allah 's blessings] upon them. Indeed, your invocations are reassurance for them. And Allah is Hearing and Knowing.\n[At-Tawba: 103]\nNow, after it has been made clear that the wealth of the poor and needy is included in our wealth and giving zakat is the only way of purifying it, the people who do not give zakat are being warned of a terrible punishment. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that the foreheads of the people who do not give zakat will be branded with hot iron rods. And the animals which were supposed to be given away as zakat but were not will trample them under their hooves and gore them with their horns again and again till Allah(swt) gives His judgement whether to send them to paradise or to hell. (See: Sahih Muslim,987)\nZakat is compulsory in the case of three types of wealth provided one whole year has passed with the wealth in the person’s possession:\n1. Gold, silver and currency.\n2. Farm produce.\n3. Trade goods.\n4. Animals reared for trade purposes like camels, cows, goats etc.\nThe minimum amount a person is required to have (Nisab) to give zakat has been decided for different things. For example a person is required to give zakat only if he has a minimum of seven and a half tolas of gold and the quantity for silver is fifty-two and a half tolas. If the currency is more than the minimum value of gold or silver, then 2 ½ percent of it needs to be given as zakat. And if the gold or silver of currency is less than this minimum amount, then zakat need not be given.\nFarm produce is of two kinds: One is the produce due to rain water. In this case one-tenth of the produce needs to be given as zakat. The second one is the produce for which artificial irrigation needs to be done. In this case one-twentieth or five percent of the harvest needs to be given as zakat. This zakat given on farm produce is called ushr.\nThe value of the trade goods is calculated and two and a half percent of that value is given as zakat.\nThe measure of the zakat on animals is different and is described in the sahih hadith. An easy way of calculating zakat is to fix a particular month for this. Then every year in that month evaluate the value of assets on which zakat is applicable and give away two and a half percent of it as zakat.\nZakat need not be given on things which are used by us. For example: house, vehicle, clothes etc. In the same way no zakat needs to be given for the plots one owns. But on selling the plot, if one year passes, then zakat needs to be given on whatever money is left.\nRegarding the gold and silver ornaments which are used, there is a difference of opinion among the scholars. But the right thing is to give zakat for them also.\nHow should the zakat be spent?\nThe Holy Quran says that the zakat has to be spent on eight kinds of people:\n﴿إِنَّمَا الصَّدَقَاتُ لِلْفُقَرَاءِ وَالْمَسَاكِينِ وَالْعَامِلِينَ عَلَيْهَا وَالْمُؤَلَّفَةِ قُلُوبُهُمْ وَفِي الرِّقَابِ وَالْغَارِمِينَ وَفِي سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ ۖ فَرِيضَةً مِّنَ اللَّـهِ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ ٦٠﴾\nZakah expenditures are only for the poor and for the needy and for those employed to collect [zakah] and for bringing hearts together [for Islam] and for freeing captives [or slaves] and for those in debt and for the cause of Allah and for the [stranded] traveler - an obligation [imposed] by Allah. And Allah is Knowing and Wise. [At-Tawba: 60]\nIn fact, zakat is a beautiful means of wiping out the financial inequality in the Islamic society and no other religion or system has such a wonderful concept. Many stories and incidents of Madina are still preserved in the historical records. One such amazing story is that the people of Madina who wanted to give zakat would be roaming the market-place with the money in their hands but they could not find any takers. The reason is as follows. It was the rule of the state that the people had to deposit the zakat for the apparent things like animals, trade goods, farm harvest etc. in the ‘Baitul-Maal’ or the government would collect it directly and then this Baitul-Maal was distributed among the poor and needy. But the zakat on the gold and silver was distributed directly by the Muslims and they could find no takers for it. In this way the concept of Zakat can permanently remove poverty from the state.\nAnd moreover Zakat is also a way of purifying the mind of man. Because his greed for more money and wealth is never satisfied and shackles him in misery; by giving away some of it to the poor, the heart experiences a peace and calm which is more valuable than the happiness he gets from all his wealth. And on top of it the fact that he is doing it for the pleasure of Allah(swt) and that his reward is waiting for him in the Hereafter adds to the pleasure and happiness. In fact, in addition to the required two and a half percent, we Muslims should try to give more as charity. In this way, zakat not only purifies the soul but also becomes a unique symbol of prosperity."],[367,"§Zakatul-Fitr\nAs mentioned previously, ‘Zakat’ means to purify. ‘Zakatul-Fitr’ also means the same thing. That is, if some slips or mistakes have happened during the fasts of Ramadan, then they can be purified with the help of ‘Zakatul-Fitr’. This zakat is also obligatory as is narrated in a sahih hadith:\nAllah's Apostle enjoined the payment of one Saa' of dates or one Saa' of barley as Zakat-ul-Fitr on every Muslim, slave or free, male or female, young or old, and he ordered that it be paid before the people went out to offer the 'Id prayer.\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1504 and Sahih Muslim, 984)\nBut Zakatul-Fitr is not obligatory upon those who do not have enough money to even buy food for themselves and their family.\nSaa’ is an ancient unit of measurement which is described in the story of Yusuf(as) (See: Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-72) which is approximately equal to three and a half kilograms. (For more information see: ‘Saa’’).\nThe right time to give this zakat is before the Id namaz so that even the poor can take part in the festivities and enjoy the Id. When we think about this zakat, we can understand that it is also a way of promoting unity in the Islamic society as the rich and the poor can live together amiably and peacefully which is the purpose of the teachings of Islam."],[368,"§Zakhkhoom\n‘Zakhkhoom’ is the name of a tree which will grow out of the depths of hell and will be full of thorns and taste extremely bitter. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِنَّهَا شَجَرَةٌ تَخْرُجُ فِي أَصْلِ الْجَحِيمِ ٦٤ طَلْعُهَا كَأَنَّهُ رُءُوسُ الشَّيَاطِينِ ٦٥﴾\nIndeed, it is a tree issuing from the bottom of the Hellfire, Its emerging fruit as if it was heads of the devils.\n[As-Saffat: 64, 65]\nThe people who go to hell will have for their sustenance this horrible tree:\n﴿إِنَّ شَجَرَتَ الزَّقُّومِ ٤٣ طَعَامُ الْأَثِيمِ ٤٤ كَالْمُهْلِ يَغْلِي فِي الْبُطُونِ ٤٥ كَغَلْيِ الْحَمِيمِ ٤٦﴾\nIndeed, the tree of zaqqum. Is food for the sinful. Like murky oil, it boils within bellies. Like the boiling of scalding water.\n[Ad-Dukhan: 43-46]\nBy the sinful people are meant the people who did not believe in Allah(swt) and were disobedient as the famous commentator Ibn-Zareer Tabri has said.\nAfter describing the unimaginable wonders and pleasures of paradise, the Holy Quran says:\n﴿أَذَٰلِكَ خَيْرٌ نُّزُلًا أَمْ شَجَرَةُ الزَّقُّومِ ٦٢ إِنَّا جَعَلْنَاهَا فِتْنَةً لِّلظَّالِمِينَ ٦٣﴾\nIs Paradise a better accommodation or the tree of zaqqum? Indeed, We have made it a torment for the wrongdoers.\n[As-Saffat: 62, 63]\n﴿ثُمَّ إِنَّكُمْ أَيُّهَا الضَّالُّونَ الْمُكَذِّبُونَ ٥١ لَآكِلُونَ مِن شَجَرٍ مِّن زَقُّومٍ ٥٢ فَمَالِئُونَ مِنْهَا الْبُطُونَ ٥٣ فَشَارِبُونَ عَلَيْهِ مِنَ الْحَمِيمِ ٥٤ فَشَارِبُونَ شُرْبَ الْهِيمِ ٥٥ هَـٰذَا نُزُلُهُمْ يَوْمَ الدِّينِ ٥٦﴾\nThen indeed you, O those astray [who are] deniers, Will be eating from trees of zaqqum. And filling with it your bellies. And drinking on top of it from scalding water. And will drink as the drinking of thirsty camels. That is their accommodation on the Day of Recompense.\n[Al-Waqi’a: 51-56]\nThat is, the dwellers of hell will pounce on the scalding water like thirsty camels, but the water will be so hot that instead of quenching their thirst it will sever their intestines. (See: Quran, Surah-47, Muhammad, Verse-15)\nSome scholars have compared the ‘Zakhkhoom’ tree with the ‘thuhar’ plant found in Tehama. But the fact is that as the ‘Zakhkhoom’ is a tree of hell, it cannot be compared to any plant or tree on earth; the example is just for giving us an idea about it. The wonders of paradise and horrors of hell cannot be compared to anything on earth nor can they be perceived or even imagined by us. All these are the matters of ‘unseen’ and believing in the unseen is part of true belief."],[369,"§Zamhareer\nSevere cold is called ‘Zamhareer’. One of the favours granted to the dwellers of paradise will be that they will neither be troubled by extreme heat nor will they have to face extreme cold. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿مُّتَّكِئِينَ فِيهَا عَلَى الْأَرَائِكِ ۖ لَا يَرَوْنَ فِيهَا شَمْسًا وَلَا زَمْهَرِيرًا ١٣﴾\n[They will be] reclining therein on adorned couches. They will not see therein any [burning] sun or [freezing] cold.\n[Ad-Dhahar: 13]\nThat is, the weather in paradise will be like spring. That is why the ones who go there will never want to go elsewhere:\n﴿خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا لَا يَبْغُونَ عَنْهَا حِوَلًا ١٠٨﴾\nWherein they abide eternally. They will not desire from it any transfer.\n[Al-Kahf: 108]"],[370,"§Zanzabeel\n‘Zanzabeel’ is the Arabic word for ginger. Among the drinks which will be served in the paradise, one will have ginger mixed in it:\n﴿وَيُسْقَوْنَ فِيهَا كَأْسًا كَانَ مِزَاجُهَا زَنجَبِيلًا ١٧﴾\nAnd they will be given to drink a cup [of wine] whose mixture is of ginger.\n[Ad-Dahar: 17]\nGinger is inherently hot. In the cool shade of paradise, the dwellers will be given a drink which has the warmth of ginger. This will not only make the drink tasty but the people who drink it will experience such joy which cannot be compared to anything on earth."],[371,"§Zikr\nThe word ‘Zikr’ has been used in the Holy Quran to convey various meanings in various contexts. A few of them are:\n1. Remembering Allah(swt), exalting His name, extolling His Sovereignty and Lordship etc. because the remembrance of Allah(swt) gives peace to the mind and soul.\nالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَتَطْمَئِنُّ قُلُوبُهُم بِذِكْرِ اللَّهِ\nThose who have believed and whose hearts are assured by the remembrance of Allah. [Ar-Ra’d: 28]\nAnd the sign of the believers is mentioned in the Holy Quran as:\nأَلَا بِذِكْرِ اللَّهِ تَطْمَئِنُّ الْقُلُوبُ\nUnquestionably, by the remembrance of Allah hearts are assured.\n[Ar-Ra’d: 28]\nIt is mentioned at another place in the Holy Quran:\nإِنَّمَا الْمُؤْمِنُونَ الَّذِينَ إِذَا ذُكِرَ اللَّهُ وَجِلَتْ قُلُوبُهُمْ\nThe believers are only those who, when Allah is mentioned, their hearts become fearful.\n[Al-Anfal: 2]\nBest time for the remembrance of Allah(swt):\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَاذْكُر رَّبَّكَ فِي نَفْسِكَ تَضَرُّعًا وَخِيفَةً وَدُونَ الْجَهْرِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ بِالْغُدُوِّ وَالْآصَالِ وَلَا تَكُن مِّنَ الْغَافِلِينَ ٢٠٥﴾\nAnd remember your Lord within yourself in humility and in fear without being apparent in speech - in the mornings and the evenings. And do not be among the heedless.\n[Al-A’raf: 205]\nAfter namaz:\nفَإِذَا قَضَيْتُمُ الصَّلَاةَ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ قِيَامًا وَقُعُودًا وَعَلَىٰ جُنُوبِكُمْ ۚ\nAnd when you have completed the prayer, remember Allah standing, sitting, or [lying] on your sides.\n[An-Nisa: 103]\nEstablishing salah is Zikr or remembrance of Allah(swt):\nوَأَقِمِ الصَّلَاةَ لِذِكْرِي\nAnd establish prayer for My remembrance.\n[Ta-Ha: 14]\nThat is why the Muslims are being commanded to remember Allah(swt) much. (See: Quran, Surah-33, Al-Ahzab, Verse-41)\nIn the Holy Quran the people who are neglectful in the remembrance of Allah(swt) are severely criticized:\n﴿وَمَن يَعْشُ عَن ذِكْرِ الرَّحْمَـٰنِ نُقَيِّضْ لَهُ شَيْطَانًا فَهُوَ لَهُ قَرِينٌ ٣٦﴾\nAnd whoever is blinded from remembrance of the Most Merciful - We appoint for him a devil, and he is to him a companion.\n[Az-Zukhruf: 36]\n﴿وَمَنْ أَعْرَضَ عَن ذِكْرِي فَإِنَّ لَهُ مَعِيشَةً ضَنكًا وَنَحْشُرُهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ أَعْمَىٰ ١٢٤ قَالَ رَبِّ لِمَ حَشَرْتَنِي أَعْمَىٰ وَقَدْ كُنتُ بَصِيرًا ١٢٥ قَالَ كَذَٰلِكَ أَتَتْكَ آيَاتُنَا فَنَسِيتَهَا ۖ وَكَذَٰلِكَ الْيَوْمَ تُنسَىٰ ١٢٦﴾\nAnd whoever turns away from My remembrance - indeed, he will have a depressed life, and We will gather him on the Day of Resurrection blind. He will say, \"My Lord, why have you raised me blind while I was [once] seeing?\" [Allah] will say, \"Thus did Our signs come to you, and you forgot them; and thus will you this Day be forgotten.\"\n[Ta-Ha: 124-126]\n2. Remembering something, as the servant who was with Musa(as) said:\nفَإِنِّي نَسِيتُ الْحُوتَ وَمَا أَنسَانِيهُ إِلَّا الشَّيْطَانُ أَنْ أَذْكُرَهُ ۚ وَاتَّخَذَ سَبِيلَهُ فِي الْبَحْرِ عَجَبًا\nIndeed, I forgot [there] the fish. And none made me forget it except Satan - that I should mention it. And it took its course into the sea amazingly\".\n[Al-Kahf: 63]\n3. Take lesson from or as a reminder:\n﴿أَوَلَا يَذْكُرُ الْإِنسَانُ أَنَّا خَلَقْنَاهُ مِن قَبْلُ وَلَمْ يَكُ شَيْئًا ٦٧﴾\nDoes man not remember that We created him before, while he was nothing?\n[Maryam: 67]\nQuran has been described as a lesson and a reminder:\n﴿مَا أَنزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْآنَ لِتَشْقَىٰ ٢ إِلَّا تَذْكِرَةً لِّمَن يَخْشَىٰ ٣﴾\nWe have not sent down to you the Qur'an that you be distressed. But only as a reminder for those who fear [Allah] [Ta-Ha: 2, 3]\n4. Quran has also been called ‘Zikr’. The disbelievers of Makkah said:\nأَأُنزِلَ عَلَيْهِ الذِّكْرُ مِن بَيْنِنَا\nHas the message been revealed to him out of [all of] us?\"\n[Sad: 8]\n﴿إِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا الذِّكْرَ وَإِنَّا لَهُ لَحَافِظُونَ ٩﴾\nIndeed, it is We who sent down the Qur'an and indeed, We will be its guardian.\n[Al-Hijr: 9]\nAllah(swt) says in the Holy Quran that He(swt) is the guardian of the Holy Quran and it is as true today as it was one thousand and five hundred years back.\n5. Ancient history – the Holy Quran has used ‘Zikr’ for this also:\n﴿وَيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَن ذِي الْقَرْنَيْنِ ۖ قُلْ سَأَتْلُو عَلَيْكُم مِّنْهُ ذِكْرًا ٨٣﴾\nAnd they ask you, [O Muhammad], about Dhul-Qarnayn. Say, \"I will recite to you about him a report (history).\"\n[Al-Kahf: 83]\nThese are a few meanings of the word ‘Zikr’ as used in the Holy Quran. The one thing which we understand from this is that the remembrance of Allah(swt) is actually ‘Zikr.’And the other meanings also in one way or the other point to the first meaning. That is why books have been written in the light of the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith which are called ‘Kitab-uz-Zikr wal Azkaar’ in which the ‘zikr’ of Allah(swt) from dawn till dusk is explained."],[372,"§Zina\n‘Zina’ which means ‘adultery’ is a social evil and the Holy Quran forbids it categorically:\n﴿وَلَا تَقْرَبُوا الزِّنَىٰ ۖ إِنَّهُ كَانَ فَاحِشَةً وَسَاءَ سَبِيلًا ٣٢﴾\nAnd do not approach unlawful sexual intercourse. Indeed, it is ever an immorality and is evil as a way.\n[Al-Isra: 32]\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith that the greatest sin is to attribute partners to Allah(swt). The second major sin is to kill one’s offspring fearing that he will eat with us and after that the next major sin is to commit adultery with the neighbour’s wife. (Sahih Bukhari, 6861 and Sahih Muslim, 86)"],[373,"§Zina(punishment)\n1. If the person committing adultery(whether it is a man or a woman) is married, then he or she will be stoned to death.\n2. If the person is not married then he will be whipped hundred times – both in the case of man and woman.\nHow will adultery be proved:\n1. The person committing adultery confesses to his or her crime four times.\n2. Or four people bear witness that they have seen the actual crime being committed. If even one of them is doubtful, then the punishment will not be applicable and the witnesses will be liable for ‘Khazaf’ or the punishment for giving false testimony. For more information on ‘Khazaf’ see: ‘Khazaf’."],[374,"§Jizya\nIn the Holy Quran, ‘Jizya’ has been described only once:\n﴿قَاتِلُوا الَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّـهِ وَلَا بِالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَلَا يُحَرِّمُونَ مَا حَرَّمَ اللَّـهُ وَرَسُولُهُ وَلَا يَدِينُونَ دِينَ الْحَقِّ مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ حَتَّىٰ يُعْطُوا الْجِزْيَةَ عَن يَدٍ وَهُمْ صَاغِرُونَ ٢٩﴾\nFight those who do not believe in Allah or in the Last Day and who do not consider unlawful what Allah and His Messenger have made unlawful and who do not adopt the religion of truth from those who were given the Scripture - [fight] until they give the jizyah willingly while they are humbled.\n[At-Tawba: 29]\nAccording to the Holy Quran, ‘jizya’ was to be collected from the ‘people of the book’ or ‘Ahle-Kitab’ and according to the sahih hadith it was to be collected from the Majoos or the fire-worshippers. ‘Jizya’ is a type of security given by the non-Muslims who are living in a Muslim kingdom. Due to this their religious freedom, wealth, honour and lives are safeguarded. This is similar to the zakat given by the Muslims so that the money can be used by the government for their security. The difference is that ‘zakat’ is a form of worship in Islam which the Muslims give cheerfully solely for the pleasure of Allah(swt) while ‘jizya’ is given by the non-Muslims for safeguarding their religious freedom. Giving ‘Jizya’ is neither for the pleasure of Allah(swt) nor for reward in the Hereafter. Therefore a non-Muslim paying ‘jizya’ will definitely think about embracing Islam and paying ‘zakat’ and seeking the pleasure of Allah(swt). It is not compulsory for the one who pays ‘Jizya’ to take part in wars; but in case he does so of his own free will, then no ‘jizya’ will be collected from him. And if the government collects ‘jizya’ from a non-Muslim and due to some reason is not able to safeguard his property or life, then the government will return the ‘jizya’."],[375,"§Zubur\n‘Zubur’ is the plural of ‘Zabur’. It means a book or religious scripture. This has been mentioned at many places in the Holy Quran. Wherever it has been used along with the word ‘Kitab’, ’Kitab’ means the ‘Taurah’ or the ‘Injeel’ and ‘Zubur’ means ‘other books’. (See: Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-184; Surah-26, Ash-Shu’ara, Verse-196; Surah-35, Fatir, Verse-25)\nAllah(swt) had given a book ‘Zabur’ to His prophet Dawood(as). The Holy Quran says:\nوَآتَيْنَا دَاوُودَ زَبُورًا\nand to David We gave the book [of Psalms].\n[An-Nisa: 163]\nThe Holy Quran says at another place:\n﴿وَرَبُّكَ أَعْلَمُ بِمَن فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۗ وَلَقَدْ فَضَّلْنَا بَعْضَ النَّبِيِّينَ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ ۖ وَآتَيْنَا دَاوُودَ زَبُورًا ٥٥﴾\nAnd your Lord is most knowing of whoever is in the heavens and the earth. And We have made some of the prophets exceed others [in various ways], and to David We gave the book [of Psalms].\n[Bani-Israel: 55]\nAnd at another place it says:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ كَتَبْنَا فِي الزَّبُورِ مِن بَعْدِ الذِّكْرِ أَنَّ الْأَرْضَ يَرِثُهَا عِبَادِيَ الصَّالِحُونَ ١٠٥﴾\nAnd We have already written in the book [of Psalms] after the [previous] mention that the land [of Paradise] is inherited by My righteous servants.\n[Al-Anbiya: 105]\nIn the Bible there is a book called Psalms (‘Zabur’) but the entire book is not ‘Zabur’. Many things have been added by people and the names of the writers have also been mentioned. But where it is mentioned that they are the original preachings, we can discern the light of the words of Allah(swt).\nThe word ‘Zubar’ is used in Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-96 of the Holy Quran which means ‘sheet’. Because the sheet is also like the papers of a book, Zul-qarnain told his army:\n﴿آتُونِي زُبَرَ الْحَدِيدِ ۖ حَتَّىٰ إِذَا سَاوَىٰ بَيْنَ الصَّدَفَيْنِ قَالَ انفُخُوا ۖ حَتَّىٰ إِذَا جَعَلَهُ نَارًا قَالَ آتُونِي أُفْرِغْ عَلَيْهِ قِطْرًا ٩٦﴾\nBring me sheets of iron\" - until, when he had leveled [them] between the two mountain walls, he said, \"Blow [with bellows],\" until when he had made it [like] fire, he said, \"Bring me, that I may pour over it molten copper.\"\n[Al-Kahf: 96]\nFor more information see: Yajooj-Majooj."]])